{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_202","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git diff --check && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"# Decode-based load probe\n\nID adds the I displacement to the raw register-file base and the registered EX/MEM result in parallel. The enabled MEM destination selects the RAM row. A pending EX writer or a matching external MEM load disables forwarding for this lookup.\n\nEach of the 1,024 entries holds a valid bit, an eight-bit page tag and the raw 32-bit word. The lookup captures the lane, immediate sign, source selector and each base's page, RAM range flag and carry. EX accepts the word when the selected base is in RAM, carry equals sign, the tag matches and the access is aligned. The same-edge RAM update check and the older-store veto protect the captured word. The lookup advances with ID/EX through memory holds. MEM receives the full forwarded byte address on every load.\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed schedule. The predictor checks the page and collisions internally and passes the match, lane and raw word to EX. The PC-indexed stride tables and their training interface have been removed.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`. All 108 cocotb tests passed, including 37 full-pipeline tests.\n- The single-retirement ALTOPS formal suite passed all 53 checks on the first run. Its 20-cycle depth is shorter than the 1,024-cycle scrub. Directed pipeline tests exercise warm hits, both end rows after reset, cross-page and pending-base misses, MMIO, and stalled store and fill collisions.\n- The selftest and all three random streams matched the reference on ready and stalled buses. CoreMark completed ten iterations between the MMIO markers in 3,153,333 cycles, with all five canonical CRCs and the validation message.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 86.378, 89.124 and 89.124 MHz. The median gives 282.63 iterations/s. It falls 0.958 MHz below the 90.082 MHz replacement threshold at this cycle count.\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/load_predictor.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
