/19d02a47/602c45c5/verify/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-wqlvhpLnk/checks/reg_ch0/model/design_smt2.smt2\n# Replay RAM probes\n\nThe predictive RAM port, its read metadata and both source-history samples advance when fetch has a usable instruction, the fence barrier is clear and ID can advance. A redirect or load-use interlock can therefore launch a probe. The read row, simultaneous fill row and fill enable are sampled together. Their comparison qualifies the response at the fabric candidate register, which holds its word and permission until issue. An issued FENCE.I or reset clears the pending permissions.\n\nThe delayed fill accepts ready, in-window bus words, including the first presentation of an interlocked consumer. A redirect discards the wrong-path fill. Row hints use the probe two samples back. The ready bus has priority over both replay sources.\n\n## Deviations from the proposal\n\nTwo existing pipeline tests stop the instruction bus for an entire trained loop. A vetoed probe can displace the only lookahead for the corrected path, leaving the PC waiting indefinitely. During a sustained miss, the idle RAM fill port reads the held PC and checks its full address. It reads the sequential successor on the validation edge so the next instruction can issue on the following clock. This recovery adds a register for the validated instruction and selection logic at fetch. A directed test covers a load consumer whose only live instruction word arrives during its interlock.\n\nThe initial placement put the ready-bus instruction mux, register-file read and branch comparison on a path ending at the ID/EX alternate-PC register. ID/EX already carries both direct successors and the prediction bit, so EX now selects the recovery address from those fields.\n\n## Local verification\n\nVerilator lint passed with all warnings enabled by the requested command. The cocotb suite passed, including all 40 pipeline cases. RVFI co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random programs with and without bus stalls. CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,069,384 marked cycles with all five canonical CRCs, the validation message and no out-of-bounds access.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
