{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml; rg -n 'implementation_notes|scratch|formal|gowin' CLAUDE.md .gitignore; ls -la formal cores/bench; ls -la test; rg -n 'latency|round|DIV/REM' cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv; rg --files cores/bench/test tools/eval\"", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 31.991\n  lut4: 2883\n  ff: 562\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261122-002-r1s1\n  updated: '2026-11-22T03:02:54.131529Z'\nCLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:12:| 2 | `rvfi_trap = 1` iff the retiring instruction is illegal per RV32IM (decoder default = illegal)             | `riscv-formal ill` check                     |\nCLAUDE.md:14:| 4 | `rvfi_order` strictly monotonic +1 per retirement across both channels combined (no gaps, no duplicates). When both channels retire in the same cycle, channel-0 order = N and channel-1 order = N+1.                                       | `riscv-formal unique` check                  |\nCLAUDE.md:15:| 5 | CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic instruction stream                                           | `riscv-formal liveness` check                |\nCLAUDE.md:16:| 5b | M-extension arithmetic produces RV32M-correct bit results                                                | cocotb `test_alu.py` + `make formal-deep`    |\nCLAUDE.md:31:- `formal/wrapper.sv`, `formal/wrapper_si\n…[3294 of 6366 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4955d6279534fa3a]…\n2297 Nov 22 04:08 _helpers.py\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  361 Nov 22 04:08 conftest.py\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 22 04:08 cosim\n12:// Latency:        6 EX cycles for DIV/REM, 1 for other instructions.\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_reclassify.py\ntools/eval/rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/test_remove_path.py\ntools/eval/test_subprocess_pgroup.py\ntools/eval/__init__.py\ntools/eval/test_slots.py\ntools/eval/test_bench_stall_gen.py\ntools/eval/test_fpga_report.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_nret.py\ntools/eval/cosim.py\ntools/eval/_slots.py\ntools/eval/test_holdout.py\ntools/eval/fpga.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_workdir_cleanup.py\ntools/eval/holdout.py\ntools/eval/test_rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/gowin.py\ntools/eval/formal.py\ntools/eval/test_process_reaper.py\ntools/eval/test_gate_sanity.py\ntools/eval/_subprocess.py\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
