{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_223","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git status --short; git diff --check; git diff --stat; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           |  70 +++++++++++----\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  50 ++++++++++-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  46 +++++++---\n cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv   |  14 +--\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       |   9 ++\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv      |  76 +++++------------\n cores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv       |   9 +-\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 175 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n 8 files changed, 334 insertions(+), 115 deletions(-)\n# Early issue for ready-base loads and stores\n\nTen CoreMark iterations with instruction and data stalls took **3,920,825 marked cycles**. The three Gowin placements reached 66.444, 65.799, and 65.799 MHz. The median gives **167.82 iterations/s**, 7.94% above the 155.48 iterations/s champion. Placement 0 used 3,444 logic cells and 717 registers.\n\n## Implementation\n\nDecode adds the signed I/S displacement to its bypassed base and captures both the sum and base readiness. EX can issue an aligned RAM access when MEM has no pending request. An accepted load captures both the raw bus word for RVFI and the extended value for forwarding. Its adjacent consumer can retire on the next cycle.\n\nA denied request advances to MEM with its effective address and replicated store data. The shared bus address register holds through backpressure. A registered pending bit gives MEM exclusive use of the port until acceptance. A misaligned access traps without a bus request or a wait for ready.\n\nThe ordinary address calculation shares the forwarded-base adder with JALR. EX qualifies the forwarding matches when decode captures the consumer. MEM/WB captures the selected destination value once for writeback. These changes shorten the forwarding path and avoid a second writeback data bank.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with all warnings enabled by the requested command.\n- Fast formal passed all 53 checks on the final implementation, with no counterexamples or retries.\n- All five cocotb suites passed, including 25 pipeline tests. Bus handshakes and RVFI checks cover signed and unsigned lanes, consecutive load-use retirement, denied requests, store-data forwarding, port contention, busy bases, wrong-path stores, MMIO, and alignment traps.\n- The selftest and three random programs matched the reference ISS with both zero-wait and stalled buses. CoreMark produced all five canonical CRCs and the validation message. The start and stop markers occurred at cycles 14,100 and 3,934,925.\n\nThe fast formal wrapper drives both ready inputs high. The directed handshake tests and stalled reference traces cover backpressure.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
