{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_155","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --numstat; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; rg '\"'^Formal:'\"' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR\"/control-formal*.log; date -u'","aggregated_output":"24\t11\tcores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n0\t2\tcores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n46\t29\tcores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n13\t9\tcores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n6\t7\tcores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n69\t17\tcores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n6\t16\tcores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n4\t3\tcores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n153\t5\tcores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n19\t0\tcores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\n# Dedicated control-transfer operands\n\nFetch keeps a zero flag, a JALR eligibility flag and bits 19:2 of the writeback result. Live and replay instructions address the metadata independently. EX, MEM and WB destinations veto stale entries. Reset values and x0 predict as zero, including a zero-offset jump to address zero.\n\nBEQ and BNE use register identity or a comparison established by current zero flags. Other comparisons use the existing counter. ID/EX captures the direction, fallthrough and complete direct target separately. EX uses an ordinary-result bypass for branch comparisons and the JALR sum. A transfer that needs an adjacent multiply inserts one bubble on an advancing cycle. Its operands then come from the write-first ID ports.\n\nThe implementation follows the fixture's configured single retirement channel. Directed tests check live and replay predictions, WB freshness, bit-one JALR faults, wrong-path stores, and one-time retirement and training after a multiply interlock.\n\nTiming measurements also motivated moving memory alignment checks into EX. EX/MEM carries the qualified request and register-write bits. The register file can present a pending write on its combinational ports while a data-bus stall holds its array write and the ID/EX operand registers.\n\nVerilator lint, the cocotb suite and five-program co-simulation passed. The stalled ten-iteration CoreMark run took 3,067,156 marked cycles, matched all five CRCs and printed “Correct operation validated.”\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 81.950, 85.827 and 85.827 MHz. The median fell below the 93.6968 MHz acceptance threshold. The limiting path in placement 1 ran from the pending load-table RAM through load-hit verification and the fetch interlock to the instruction replay RAM.\n\nLocal ALTOPS formal has passed 52 of 53 checks. The forward-PC check is still running.\nSun Nov 22 17:10:24 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
