.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261122-002-r11s1\n  updated: '2026-11-22T12:46:35.718391Z'\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r1s0 (regression, +32.67%): Parallel radix-4 trials raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.44 to 7.22 MHz, but chaining 16 remainder selections in one EX cycle kept it below the multicycle divider’s 32 MHz.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r1s1 (improvement, +487.71%): Limiting the restoring divider to eight quotient steps per clock s\n…[12897 of 15969 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:929fa17445fa35a1]…\nules the path crosses (in order), from Gowin's timing report.\"\"\"\n114:        return {\"placement_failed\": True, \"fmax_mhz\": None, \"reason\": \"no Fmax in timing report\"}\n133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n137:            proc.wait(timeout=BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC)\n155:    # Plain threads and blocking waits, no asyncio: agents run `make timing`\n158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\n162:                \"reason\": f\"Gowin build timeout after {BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC}s\"}\n173:    with eval_slot(\"gowin\"), ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=len(options)) as ex:\n175:                          Path(gen_dir) / f\"gowin_p{p}\", env) for p in options]\n200:    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\n214:                                wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\", options=opts)\n221:        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
