{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml; rg -n 'implementation_notes|sandbox|nret' CLAUDE.md .gitignore; ls -la formal cores/bench/test; cat cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 47.7\n  lut4: 2984\n  ff: 601\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261122-002-r2s1\n  updated: '2026-11-22T03:36:04.686169Z'\n.gitignore:14:# status flags the symlink as untracked and sandbox check trips).\n.gitignore:22:# and the scribe-phase sandbox check rolls back the scribe's commit.\n.gitignore:30:# sandbox check in tools/agents/hypothesis.py rolls back the next slot's\n.gitignore:38:# into Phase 1 and Phase 2. Untracked so the orchestrator's sandbox check\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\nCLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:47:Enforcement (`tools/tournament.py:run_slot`, `tools/sandbox.py`): the\nCLAUDE.md:53:it built itself. Any mismatch is `broken: sandbox_violation`.\nCLAUDE.md:58:`cores/<TARGET>/test/test_*.py`. The agent's `implementation_notes.md`\nCLAUDE.md:59:lives at `cores/<TARGET>/implementation_notes.md` (gitignored). The\nCLAUDE.md:68:set determined by `core.yaml`'s `nret` field — only `io_rvfi_*_0`\nCLAUDE.md:69:fields for `nret: 1`; both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` for\nCLAUDE.md:70:`nret: 2`\n…[3000 of 6072 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c949b60fc504f1bd]…\ns.\nmodule forward_unit (\n  input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rs1,\n  input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rs2,\n  input  logic [4:0] ex_mem_rd,\n  input  logic       ex_mem_w_en,\n  input  logic [4:0] mem_wb_rd,\n  input  logic       mem_wb_w_en,\n  output logic [1:0] fwd_rs1,\n  output logic [1:0] fwd_rs2\n);\n\n  // Yosys's Verilog frontend rejects SV-style `function … return …`,\n  // so the per-rs selection is open-coded in two always_comb blocks.\n  always_comb begin\n    if      (ex_mem_w_en && ex_mem_rd != 5'b0 && ex_mem_rd == id_ex_rs1) fwd_rs1 = 2'd1;\n    else if (mem_wb_w_en && mem_wb_rd != 5'b0 && mem_wb_rd == id_ex_rs1) fwd_rs1 = 2'd2;\n    else                                                                  fwd_rs1 = 2'd0;\n  end\n\n  always_comb begin\n    if      (ex_mem_w_en && ex_mem_rd != 5'b0 && ex_mem_rd == id_ex_rs2) fwd_rs2 = 2'd1;\n    else if (mem_wb_w_en && mem_wb_rd != 5'b0 && mem_wb_rd == id_ex_rs2) fwd_rs2 = 2'd2;\n    else                                                                  fwd_rs2 = 2'd0;\n  end\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
