{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg && ls -la /opt && rg -n 'TMPDIR|GOWIN|smp|jobs|timeout|elf' tools/eval/{gowin,formal,cosim}.py\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 20 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 01:00 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 gowin\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:57 hwe-python\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 hwe-toolchain\ntools/eval/cosim.py:4:  1. Full RVFI trace cosim for selftest and any other small ELF — every\ntools/eval/cosim.py:7:     of coremark.elf is skipped because the Python reference is ~10⁴× slower\ntools/eval/cosim.py:48:def run_one(elf: Path, sim_bin: str, worktree: str, env: dict | None = None,\ntools/eval/cosim.py:55:       \n…[3197 of 6269 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0a5fe448f58fa014]…\n from tools.eval._slots import eval_jobs, eval_slot\ntools/eval/formal.py:138:            if eval_jobs():\ntools/eval/formal.py:139:                env = {**env, \"JOBS\": eval_jobs()}\ntools/eval/formal.py:145:                    timeout=2700,  # 45 min ceiling for all ~45 checks running in parallel via make -j\ntools/eval/formal.py:168:                'failed_check': 'timeout',\ntools/eval/formal.py:169:                'detail': (f'run_all.sh exceeded {e.timeout}s wall-clock'\ntools/eval/gowin.py:22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:137:            proc.wait(timeout=BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC)\ntools/eval/gowin.py:162:                \"reason\": f\"Gowin build timeout after {BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC}s\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
