{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git status --short; git check-ignore -v cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md | tail -10'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n D cores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nEX/MEM records the handshake, the early-load select, the raw response, and the extended value alongside the ALU result. Only unfinished EX loads interlock with their immediate consumers. MEM retries pending transfers, suppresses requests for accepted transfers, and retires misaligned accesses with a trap and zero masks regardless of bus readiness.\n\nEX and MEM share one load-extension circuit at the data port. The registered owner selects its width and signedness. MEM selects the early load, pending load, or ALU result in parallel and writes it directly to the register file on completion. The same edge latches that result and the matching RVFI packet, eliminating the separate WB mux. The configured single RVFI channel reports each retirement.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator passed the requested lint command with zero warnings.\n- All five cocotb suites passed, including 27 pipeline tests. The added checks cover each load width, adjacent consumers, a denied halfword store with a forwarded value, a contending load, consecutive MMIO transfers, misalignment on a denied bus, and a squashed store. The branch-bypass and ordered-loop tests retain their exact fetch sequences.\n- Selftest and all three frozen random programs matched the Python ISS on ready buses and with both stall generators enabled.\n- CoreMark ran between marker cycles 11,416 and 3,184,410, reached EBREAK in bounds, and printed `Correct operation validated.` The seed, list, matrix, state, and final CRCs were `e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, and `fcaf`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
