{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path; print(Path(\\\"cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\\\").read_text())' && cmp \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/bench-nonzero/test/test_pipeline.py\" cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py'","aggregated_output":"# Adjacent-producer forwarding\n\nEX registers three bank selects for each operand on the ID/EX capture edge. Decode supplies the register matches and excludes x0. EX qualifies each match with the producer's resolved write permission and multiply class. A faulting JAL or JALR clears that permission, so its consumer uses the operand captured in ID.\n\nEach source selects between the captured operand and the raw ordinary result in parallel with selecting the low or high product. The registered multiply match chooses the final operand for address generation, branch resolution, arithmetic, stores, divide launch and RVFI. MEM uses its existing bank enables for writeback. Missed and misaligned dependent loads take the existing load-use interlock.\n\nI removed the superseded forwarding module and its cocotb source-list entry. The new regression chains all four multiply instructions through rs1-only, rs2-only and two-source dependencies. It checks store data through three wait cycles, a faulting JALR shadowing an ordinary write, a multiply targeting x0, and retirement spacing.\n\n## Local results\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`. All 103 cocotb tests passed across five suites.\n- Selftest and the three random programs matched the reference RVFI traces with ready and stalled buses.\n- Ten stalled CoreMark iterations took 3,132,302 marker-to-marker cycles. The five CRCs were `e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a` and `fcaf`. UART reported “Correct operation validated.”\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 76.764, 78.353 and 78.353 MHz. The median gives **250.15 iterations/s**, 9.23% above 229.00. Resource use was 3,950 logic cells, 743 registers, nine block RAMs and two DSPs.\n- The median placement fell 1.330 MHz short of the scratch result. Its longest reported setup path starts at the fetch successor RAM and ends at the load predictor's lookup-valid register.\n- Fast ALTOPS formal has passed 52 checks. The register-consistency check is running.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
