{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml; rg -n 'implementation_notes|formal|gowin|cosim|tmpdir' .gitignore CLAUDE.md; ls -la formal cores/bench cores/bench/test; rg --files test\"", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 5.442\n  lut4: 12312\n  ff: 460\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: baseline-bench-29140aa\n  updated: '2026-11-22T02:35:52.532182Z'\nCLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:12:| 2 | `rvfi_trap = 1` iff the retiring instruction is illegal per RV32IM (decoder default = illegal)             | `riscv-formal ill` check                     |\nCLAUDE.md:14:| 4 | `rvfi_order` strictly monotonic +1 per retirement across both channels combined (no gaps, no duplicates). When both channels retire in the same cycle, channel-0 order = N and channel-1 order = N+1.                                       | `riscv-formal unique` check                  |\nCLAUDE.md:15:| 5 | CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic instruction stream                                           | `riscv-formal liveness` check                |\nCLAUDE.md:16:| 5b | M-extension arithmetic produces RV32M-correct bit results                                                | cocotb `test_alu.py` + `make formal-deep`    |\nCLAUDE.md:31:- `formal/wrapper.sv`, `formal/wrapper_s\n…[3046 of 6118 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8bb9b23f53af1813]…\n03:44 test_alu.py\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 11218 Nov 22 03:44 test_decoder.py\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2478 Nov 22 03:44 test_imm_gen.py\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 13700 Nov 22 03:44 test_pipeline.py\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  2626 Nov 22 03:44 test_reg_file.py\n\nformal:\ntotal 56\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 22 03:44 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 22 03:44 ..\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2630 Nov 22 03:44 checks-deep.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2658 Nov 22 03:44 checks.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  1455 Nov 22 03:44 checks_si.cfg\nlrwxrwxrwx+  1 nobody nogroup    68 Nov 22 03:44 riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep5/formal/riscv-formal\n-rwxrwx---+  1 nobody nogroup 10597 Nov 22 03:44 run_all.sh\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  4615 Nov 22 03:44 wrapper.sv\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2863 Nov 22 03:44 wrapper_si.sv\ntest/cosim/reference.py\ntest/cosim/main.cpp\ntest/cosim/build.sh\ntest/cosim/run_cosim.py\ntest/conftest.py\ntest/_helpers.py\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
