{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --check'","aggregated_output":"# Fetch-stage branch prediction\n\nFetch predicts legal conditional branches using 128 two-bit saturating counters indexed by PC[8:2]. Reset starts a 128-clock sweep that sets each counter to weakly not taken. Fetch continues during the sweep, including direct JAL prediction. A taken prediction requires a word-aligned target in the 1 MiB instruction memory.\n\nID carries one direction bit into EX. EX uses the forwarded operands to resolve the transfer, updates the counter on each advancing conditional branch after initialization, and recovers from either kind of direction mismatch. Recovery overrides an instruction-memory wait. A data-memory freeze holds the prediction with its instruction and defers both training and recovery. The resolved successor also drives RVFI. JALR resolves in EX.\n\nEX sends only the seven PC index bits needed for training. The hazard unit expresses the memory stall as an independent combinational assignment so that EX can qualify recovery without a combinational dependency on the fetch flush.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator passed the requested wildcard-order lint command with zero warnings. A guarded include in `core.sv` makes the bundle types available in that source order.\n- All 81 cocotb cases passed. Pipeline tests cover initialization, warmed taken branches and loop exit, aliasing, a branch frozen behind a load, recovery during an instruction-memory wait, wrong-path stores, and target legality. They check fetch addresses and RVFI successor and order.\n- Co-simulation passed selftest and three random programs against the ISS, each with and without bus stalls. Under both stalls, ten CoreMark iterations ran from marker cycle 14,996 to 4,217,268 for **4,202,272 bracketed cycles**. All five canonical CRCs matched, UART reported “Correct operation validated.”, and the simulator reported zero out-of-bounds accesses.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
