{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git check-ignore cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --check'","aggregated_output":"# Fetch prediction from ready operands\n\nTen marked CoreMark iterations took 4,151,767 cycles with both bus stalls enabled. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 48.948, 50.920 and 50.920 MHz. The median gives 122.65 iterations/s, 15.49% above the supplied baseline of 106.20 iterations/s.\n\n## Implementation\n\nFetch reads both operands from the write-first register file and bypasses EX/MEM results. A matching ID/EX writer always makes the operand busy, as does an EX/MEM load. Fetch compares ready operands for all six legal branch conditions. A busy branch uses the high bit of its two-bit counter at PC[8:2].\n\nBranches and JAL share a PC-relative adder. Zero-offset JALR uses its ready base with bit zero cleared. Fetch checks alignment and the 1 MiB instruction window before predicting a transfer. EX uses the forwarded operands for architectural resolution and recovers on a direction mismatch.\n\nThe table uses one write port for the 128-cycle reset sweep and subsequent training. ID/EX holds the prediction and counter snapshot through freezes. Raw instruction bits reach decode directly, and a kill clears the ID/EX control word and valid bit. The bench core retains its configured single RVFI channel.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with all requested warnings enabled.\n- All 93 cocotb cases passed, including 23 pipeline cases. The standard formal bound is 20 cycles, so the directed loop test runs past the 128-cycle sweep and checks trained predictions, counter saturation, two consecutive decrements and loop exit.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the reference RVFI trace with and without bus stalls.\n- CoreMark reached EBREAK with all five expected CRCs and the validation message. The start and stop markers occurred at cycles 14,722 and 4,166,489. The simulator reported zero out-of-bounds accesses.\ncores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
