{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261122-001-r14s0.last cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r14s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r14s0\ntitle: Encode the replay row so sequential fetch needs no address adder\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On the champion's 89.419 MHz median Gowin placement, the fetch PC selects\n  an exception-table entry, checks its tag, selects a replay row and tests\n  that row for a concurrent fill before read_ok_q can settle. Duplicating\n  the instruction RAM in round 12 preserved the 3,061,795 marked cycles\n  but reduced median Fmax. The address encoding can shorten this path while\n  retaining one synchronous instruction RAM.\nhypothesis: |\n  Place the instruction for word address Q at physical row (Q - 2) modulo\n  1024. A sequential second successor of word P then lives at row P.\n  Use a 256-entry distributed RAM indexed by the low eight word-PC bits.\n  Each entry directly supplies the low eight physical row bits and a\n  two-bit XOR correction to the source's upper two row bits. Initialize\n  entry i to low row i and correction zero. On observing accepted issues\n  P, B, Q with a live in-window word at Q, train P's entry with the low\n  eight bits of Q's physical row and the XOR of its upper two bits with\n  P's upper two bits. Register the fill address and training data before\n  writing. The lookup now costs one table read and at most a two-input\n  XOR per address bit. Aliasing can waste a probe, but the full destination\n  PC tag still determines whether the returned instruction can issue.\n\n  Capture the physical read and concurrent write rows at the RAM edge and\n  compare them in the following issue interval, before enabling the fabric\n  candidate. This removes collision detection from address setup. Compare\n  both marked cycles and median Fmax. At 3,061,795 cycles the 4.6 percent\n  replacement margin requires more than 93.53 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Reindex the word RAM and replace the tagged exception mux with the\n      encoded row table. Advance source history and both read stages on\n      accepted issue. Carry the sampled collision metadata across holds.\n      Preserve ready-bus priority, the full in-window PC check, and reset\n      and FENCE.I scrubbing of both tables and all outstanding permissions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise sequential replay across the modulo-1024 wrap and alternating\n      sources sharing a row-table index. Check retired PCs and words on\n      instruction waits, including a simultaneous physical-row fill followed\n      by a hold and a code-store/FENCE.I sequence.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
