offset come from instruction bits 31:25. Opcode bit 5 selects\n      instruction bits 11:7 for stores or 24:20 for loads. Capture the sum\n      into ID/EX and register the existing rs1 readiness in parallel on the\n      same operand-capture edge. Expose the decode sum to the bus a\n…[2063 of 5135 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:499e9164973bd073]…\npath for\n      busy-base, misaligned, MMIO and retried accesses. The shared address\n      register in core now supplies the physical bus address.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check consecutive retirements for a ready-base load and its consumer,\n      with signed byte and halfword lanes. Deny the first early handshake\n      and check the stable retry, original load-use interlock and exactly\n      one accepted transfer. Exercise adjacent early store/load to one\n      address, a forwarded store value, contention with an older stalled\n      access, a pending base writer, a wrong-path store, MMIO and\n      misalignment. In the existing load-bypass branch test, deny the second\n      load's early attempt once to exercise its MEM bypass. In the ordered\n      loop test, deny the early request plus the three existing MEM waits.\n      This preserves the checked fetch sequences and wrong-path store\n      assertions. Check accepted transactions alongside RVFI data, masks,\n      trap and order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
