{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 4 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Predict equality branches from decode operands and register the recovery PC\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The champion fetches PC+4 and discards one fetch slot per taken transfer.\\nIts 4,491,485 marked CoreMark cycles include 294,425 conditional branches\\nwith a nonsequential successor. Earlier bimodal branch and JAL prediction\\nsaved 289,213 cycles. The champion now assembles both operands in decode,\\nso fetch can also predict data-dependent equality branches and register\\njumps using values the datapath already provides.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion fetches PC+4 and discards one fetch slot per taken transfer.\\nIts 4,491,485 marked CoreMark cycles include 294,425 conditional branches\\nwith a nonsequential successor. Earlier bimodal branch and JAL prediction\\nsaved 289,213 cycles. The champion now assembles both operands in decode,\\nso fetch can also predict data-dependent equality branches and register\\njumps using values the datapath already provides.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give fetch one 32-bit equality comparator. For a legal BEQ or BNE whose\\nsources are both ready, use the comparison of the existing MEM/WB-bypassed\\nID operands. A source is ready when the instruction in ID/EX has no pending\\nwrite to that nonzero register. For ordered branches and busy-source\\nequality branches, use a PC-indexed table of 128 two-bit saturating counters.\\nPredict direct JAL taken. For legal zero-offset JALR with a ready rs1,\\nuse rs1 with bit zero cleared. Require word alignment and a target inside\\nthe 1 MiB instruction window for a taken prediction. Default to PC+4.\\n\\nForm PC+4 and the direct B/J target during fetch. Register the unused\\ndirect successor at issue so EX has the recovery address before it resolves\\nthe condition. A predicted JALR target is exact because its base is ready\\nand its displacement is zero. A single direction bit therefore suffices\\nfor recovery. EX still resolves every control transfer with the true\\nforwarded operands and prese\n…[30624 of 33696 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:aaff0917e4754c8a]…\novement\", \"fitness\": 184.82, \"delta_pct\": 18.87, \"vs_baseline\": 1424.92, \"fmax_mhz\": 62.73, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3394055, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3393, \"ff\": 689, \"seeds\": [60.131, 62.73, 62.73], \"perturbations\": [[0, 60.131, 11], [1, 62.73, 21], [2, 62.73, 21]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_21_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -11.63, \"arrival_ns\": 21.925, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T04:56:31.741319Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r5s2 (improvement, +18.87%): Repeated instruction pairs on sequential and taken paths let fetch bypass `imemReady` stalls by replaying the issuing PC's saved successor word when its address matched the requested PC, saving 770,138 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
