{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r6s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261122-001-r6s0\ntitle: Issue same-page RAM accesses in EX with a 12-bit address adder\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  A load whose base is ready in decode still waits for MEM and stalls an\n  adjacent consumer. Round 5 demonstrated that EX can use an idle data\n  port. On the current successor-table core, the opportunity is to do\n  this with a short decode adder while retaining the full address path\n  for page crossings, dependent bases and MMIO.\nhypothesis: |\n  In ID, add the low 12 bits of the bypassed base to the raw 12-bit I/S\n  displacement. The unsigned carry equals the displacement sign bit\n  exactly when the signed addition stays in the base's 4 KiB page.\n  For a ready base in the 1 MiB RAM window, that equality certifies the\n  complete address by concatenating the base page with the low sum.\n  Register the candidate on the data port. In EX, a valid, naturally\n  aligned load or store may use it when no older request owns the port.\n\n  An accepted load supplies its extended value through the existing\n  adjacent-EX bypass on the following cycle. An accepted store writes\n  once. A denied early request continues in MEM at the architectural\n  address with the same enables and store data. This removes load-use\n  bubbles and gives a memory operation an extra opportunity to handshake.\n\n  A scratch prototype saved 221,062 of the champion's 3,394,055 marked\n  cycles over ten CoreMark iterations with randomized waits on both buses. At\n  3,172,993 cycles the acceptance threshold requires a median above\n  61.341 MHz. Gowin placements reached 62.685, 63.231 and 63.231 MHz,\n  yielding 199.28 iterations/s, 7.82% above 184.82. Placement 0 used\n  3,715 logic cells and 789 registers. All five CRCs and the validation\n  string matched, and all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks passed.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Form disp from instr[31:25] and either instr[11:7] for S-type or\n      instr[24:20] for I-type. Sum the two zero-extende\n…[1157 of 4229 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:76f662e81d774122]…\ne the saved architectural address for alignment, masks and RVFI.\n      Format the saved raw word for an early-completed load or the live\n      word for an outstanding MEM load. Preserve the MEM-to-ID bypass,\n      writeback, and raw RVFI data. The shared register in core drives\n      the physical bus address.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check adjacent retirement after a same-page load, and the fallback\n      bubble for 0x0ffc + 4 and 0x1000 - 4. Check subword extension and a\n      forwarded halfword store held across denial, including stable\n      address, masks, data and exactly one accepted transfer. Cover\n      same-page negative offsets, pending bases, MMIO and misalignment.\n      Check the accepted bus transactions as well as the RVFI record.\n      In the existing branch-bypass\n      test deny the second load's early attempt. In the ordered-loop\n      test deny the early attempt plus the three existing MEM waits to\n      retain its recovery trace and wrong-path store checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
