{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261122-001-r7s0.log').open():\n try: item=json.loads(line).get('item',{})\n except ValueError: continue\n output=item.get('aggregated_output','')\n if item.get('type')=='agent_message':\n  print(item.get('text','')[-1800:])\n elif '62.015' in output and len(output)<40000:\n  hits=[s for s in output.splitlines() if any(v in s for v in ('62.015','path 1:', 'critical path', 'repair', 'median'))]\n  print('\\\\n'.join(s[:440] for s in hits[:8]))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"I’ll inspect the checkout, implement the registered multiply path, then run the requested checks and record the results in `implementation_notes.md`.\nThe stalled CoreMark run passed its CRC checks and measured 29,155 repairs across 93,960 multiplies. The bracket took 3,151,480 cycles, up 0.93%, which puts the acceptance clock at 67.77 MHz. All three Gowin placements are running.\n  path 1: 21.91 ns, 48 cells, cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s -> cpu/u_if/pc_word_7_s1\nplace_option 1: Fmax 62.015 MHz, 18 logic levels; logic 4059, registers 749, LUT-RAM 88, BSRAM 9, DSP 2\n  path 1: 21.419 ns, 46 cells, cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s -> cpu/u_if/pc_word_13_s1\nplace_option 2: Fmax 62.015 MHz, 18 logic levels; logic 4059, registers 749, LUT-RAM 88, BSRAM 9, DSP 2\n  path 1: 21.419 ns, 46 cells, cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s -> cpu/u_if/pc_word_13_s1\nscore Fmax (median): 62.015 MHz\ngowin_p1 62.015\ngowin_p2 62.015\nThe first implementation reached a median of 62.015 MHz. Fetch and divider feedback are now the two slowest paths. I’ll measure one smaller repair circuit that keeps an already-correct operand in its input register and updates each operand that needs forwarding.\nThe dedicated registers with a common repair enable gave the best median Fmax. I restored that version and am rerunning lint, formal, co-simulation, and timing on the final source.\n[(1, 62.015, {'from': 'cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_word_13_s1', 'slack_ns': -11.125, 'arrival_ns': 21.419, 'logic_cells': 46, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_rf', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_if']}), (2, 62.015, {'from': 'cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_word_13_s1', 'slack_ns': -11.125, 'arrival_ns': 21.419, 'logic_cells': 46, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_rf', 'cpu', \n62.015 4059 749 2\nRegistered multiply inputs passed all 53 formal checks, 104 cocotb tests, and co-simulation.\n\nCoreMark measured **29,155 repair cycles** across 93,960 multiplies. Median Fmax was **62.015 MHz**, below the **67.77 MHz** required at 3,151,480 cycles. Throughput fell 4.29% to 196.78 iterations/s.\n\n[Implementation notes](./cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
