{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r10s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r10s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261122-002-r10s1\ntitle: Register execute corrections at the issue boundary\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  In a reproduction of the champion's 85.513 MHz median placement, the longest path runs from the registered multiplier through rs1 forwarding, the load-address carry chain and tag comparison to an ID/EX control bit. Placement 0 ends a similar path at the fetch replay RAM. Both exist because decode waits for EX to decide whether a younger instruction may enter ID/EX. The load and its consumer still occupy separate pipeline stages on the following cycle, when the machine has a registered hit verdict.\nhypothesis: |\n  Admit the younger instruction to ID/EX on the normal advancing edge. Capture one bit per operand marking a match to the older load's nonzero destination. On a verified hit, the consumer executes immediately through the ordinary adjacent bypass. On a miss with a matching operand, hold that consumer until MEM completes the load. On the completion edge, replace each matching operand with the extended load value, clear its forwarding selects and send a bubble to EX/MEM. A trapping load preserves the captured register values. The consumer then executes exactly once. Suppress its branch recovery, predictor training, divide launch, memory requests and retirement throughout repair.\n\n  Register the recovery PC separately from ordinary fetch advancement. Capture the alternate target while no recovery is outstanding. A registered redirect selects the corrected PC on the next cycle and keeps it stable through fetch waits. Qualify link forwarding with jump alignment. Clock the physical instruction replay RAM every cycle. A delayed accepted-issue bit identifies the response to keep in a holding register if issue pauses. Advance candidate validity, collision metadata and two-issue history only on accepted correct-path issues. Only a surviving FENCE.I may invalidate replay state and serialize fresh fetch behind an older store.\n\n  A scratch prototype targets the champion's 3,131,081-cycle marker interval. Gowin placement 1 reached 88.975 MHz. At that cycle count 89.447 MHz is needed for replacement. The remaining margin depends on the placement median and the implementation of the registered correction paths.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Capture adjacent load dependencies at issue, derive repair from the registered MEM verdict, preserve the consumer across waits and route the completing MEM value to both operand patch ports.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Replace the combinational EX load-hit interlock with a hold for the registered dependent miss. Allow the older memory operation to complete during the hold.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Separate control capture from the valid bit that kills a wrong-path packet. On the repair edge update only the matching operands of the held instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Emit a bubble during repair and clear stale forwarding selects on completion. Separate jump-link write permission from the branch comparator and deliver the resolved target to the recovery register.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Register recovery selection separately from ordinary fetch advancement, hold the corrected PC through stalls, and stage free-running replay RAM responses against accepted issue history. Invalidate on the surviving fence in EX.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check hit and miss consumers, both sources matching, a trapping misaligned load, and a stalled load feeding a branch or divide. Check redirect through an imem wait and a killed FENCE.I. The load-to-branch trace should hold the successor PC during repair since the branch has already entered ID/EX. Check all retired values and wrong-path store suppression.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
