{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r12s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Commit instruction replay reads one clock after issue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,061,795 cycles for ten marked iterations. On placement 0,\n  its longest path runs from the adjacent producer's result to the clock enable\n  of fetch history. On placements 1 and 2 the longest path ends at read_ok_q.\n  A load-hit check or branch correction can arrive late because the replay\n  RAM, its candidate register and the two-PC history all advance on issue.\nhypothesis: |\n  Separate probing the instruction RAM from committing a probe to the replay\n  stream. Clock the read port on every edge and register the one-bit issue\n  decision alongside the response. At the following edge, use the previous\n  issue bit to save the last accepted response through any intervening holds.\n  Apply the same scheme at the candidate boundary so the live replay word\n  still comes from the probe made exactly two accepted issues earlier. Carry\n  collision permission with each word. Shift the training history one clock\n  later, using the sampled PC, exception match and registered issue bit.\n  This removes the same-cycle backpressure path into the physical block RAM\n  and wide replay state while retaining single-cycle issue on a warmed loop.\n\n  Reset and an issued FENCE.I invalidate live and parked responses and cancel\n  outstanding fills. A killed instruction cannot train history or trigger a\n  fence. Keep the full-PC tag check, live bus priority and store/fence ordering.\n  At the champion's cycle count the median must exceed 93.53 MHz to replace it.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Launch a physical read every clock, register issue and collision metadata,\n      and use last-accepted response storage at the two replay stages. Advance\n      exception training with registered issue and its matching source PC.\n      Preserve the ordering of fills, invalidations and read/write collision checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      On a warmed sequence introduce gaps between the first, second and third\n      issued instructions. Check the exact RVFI PCs and data as consecutive\n      stalled fetches consume the saved words. Exercise a redirect, delayed-fill\n      collision and FENCE.I while a response is parked.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
