{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if 'r5s' in line:\n  print(str(d)[:12000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261122-001-r5s0', 'title': 'Issue ready-base loads and stores one cycle early', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'motivation': 'The champion waits for EX/MEM before presenting every data request. When\\ndecode already has the correct base and the older instruction leaves the\\ndata port idle, that costs a bus opportunity. An adjacent load consumer\\nalso takes a bubble even when RAM could have returned the word in EX.\\n', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The champion waits for EX/MEM before presenting every data request. When\\ndecode already has the correct base and the older instruction leaves the\\ndata port idle, that costs a bus opportunity. An adjacent load consumer\\nalso takes a bubble even when RAM could have returned the word in EX.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Compute the effective address in decode from its bypassed rs1 and the\\nsigned I/S displacement. A valid, aligned RAM load or store with a ready\\nbase can use the idle data port in EX. On acceptance, capture the result\\nand mark the access complete. A dependent consumer can immediately use\\nthe registered load result through the existing EX/MEM forwarding path.\\nAn outstanding older access takes priority. A denied early request\\ncontinues in MEM at the same address with the same lanes and store data.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations with both bus stalls and the\\nfive canonical CRCs in 3,920,825 marked cycles, down from 4,164,193.\\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 65.170, 65.099 and 65.099 MHz.\\nThe median gives 166.03 iterations/s, 6.79% above the 155.48 champion.\\nAt this cycle count the acceptance threshold requires more than 63.765 MHz.\\nPlacement option 0 used 3,635 logic cells and 749 registers. The prototype\\npassed all 53 fast formal checks, all five cocotb suites with updated\\npipeline coverage, and the selftest and three random reference traces\\nwith and without bus stalls.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 7, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add the signed 12-bit offs\n…[6611 of 9683 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e8b2e9c85fd01d8b]…\n'fitness': 167.82, 'delta_pct': 7.94, 'vs_baseline': 1284.65, 'fmax_mhz': 65.799, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3920825, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 3444, 'ff': 717, 'seeds': [66.444, 65.799, 65.799], 'perturbations': [[0, 66.444, 11], [1, 65.799, 22], [2, 65.799, 22]], 'lutram': 40, 'bsram': 4, 'dsp': 6, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.ctrl.mem_read_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_21_s0', 'slack_ns': -10.05, 'arrival_ns': 20.344, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'logic_levels': 11, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-22T05:11:54.663266Z', 'slot': 0, 'round_id': 5, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r5s0 (regression, +7.94%): Issuing ready-base RAM accesses in EX when the data port was free let EX/MEM forward accepted loads without a load-use bubble, saving 243,368 CoreMark cycles versus 770,138 saved by predicting the next instruction during fetch stalls.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
