{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261122-002-r5s1.last cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261122-003-r5s2.last'","aggregated_output":"Wrote and schema-validated the [structural hypothesis](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-002-r5s1-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r5s1.yaml). It gives decode a second instruction source that replays previously issued sequences during fetch stalls.\n\nThe scratch prototype reached **178.57 CoreMark iterations/s**, **14.85% above the champion**. Ten iterations took 3,493,911 cycles at a median Gowin Fmax of 62.392 MHz. All five CoreMark CRCs matched, and all 53 standard formal checks and 24 pipeline tests passed.Wrote and schema-validated the [predictor hypothesis](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-003-r5s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r5s2.yaml).\n\nThe 512-entry predictor remembers which instruction followed each issuing PC. During an instruction-bus stall, it can supply that word when its saved address matches the requested PC.\n\nThe isolated prototype reached **180.66 CoreMark iterations/s**, **16.20% above the champion**, at a median 61.317 MHz. It saved 770,138 marked cycles using two additional block RAMs. All five CoreMark CRCs, 53 fast formal checks, and 94 cocotb cases passed.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
