{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261122-003-r11s2.log'):\n try:d=json.loads(l)['item']\n except (ValueError,KeyError):continue\n o=d.get('aggregated_output','')\n if 'reg_q.mem_addr_16_s0' in o and ('read_row_q_9_s0' in o) and ('u_mem/' in o or 'modules' in o):\n  i=o.find('reg_q.mem_addr_16_s0')\n  print(d.get('id'),o[i:i+2000])\n if d.get('id')=='item_164' and o: print(o[-2400:])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"5 minutes)\nSBY 12:44:16 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:02  Checking assertions in step 20..\nSBY 12:45:16 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:02  waiting for solver (1 minute)\n  \"elfs_tested\": 5\n}\n\n============================== 5 passed in 16.53s ==============================\n# Producer-guided load lookup and consumer refetch\n\nID uses the preceding LW's raw candidate word or the low 12-bit sum of the producer's registered operands to select the row for displacements from −4 through +3. Other pending bases use the PC-indexed stride. A ready base uses the write-first register value plus the displacement. Stride training writes the history one cycle after resolution.\n\nEX forwards the provisionally extended value and captures the coherence permission, word tag, raw data and effective byte address. MEM checks the complete word address, RAM window and alignment. A failed check causes one refetch of an adjacent consumer when the older load completes. The discarded execution cannot retire, store, train a branch or start a divide. A trapping load leaves the destination register available with its previous value.\n\nThe instruction lookahead advances once per consumer across a retry. When the refetch bus stalls, the discarded instruction can supply the word at its own in-window PC. This preserves forward progress in the existing warmed-loop test with the instruction bus held low.\n\nThe first formal run passed 52 checks and failed liveness. Its counterexample refetched a DIVU after a missed load, leaving 11 cycles between retirements against the 10-cycle bound. The divider now enters MEM on its final RUN edge and supplies its registered result during DONE. ID can read that result on the write-first ports. All 53 checks passed after this correction.\n\nDirected tests cover a warmed irregular pointer chain, a stale producer operand, crossing and non-crossing byte displacements, page aliases, store collisions, and a misaligned load feeding a store. They check completed bus transfers, raw and extended RVFI data, PC refetch counts, retirement order and retirement spacing.\n\nVerilator lint passed. Selftest and three random programs matched the reference RVFI traces on ready and stalled buses. Ten CoreMark iterations took 3,063,003 marked cycles, from 11,745 to 3,074,748. All five expected CRCs and the validation banner were present, and the harness reported zero out-of-bounds accesses.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
