{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 1 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r15s1\", \"title\": \"Fold RV32M execution into one registered DSP multiplier\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Round 14 exposed two expensive RV32M paths. A registered product can feed\\nthe next EX result through the operand muxes, and the wide divider chains\\ntwo quotient-digit decisions per clock. The timed loop executes 93,960\\nMULs and no DIV or REM. Putting division on the same DSP used for MUL\\ncould remove both divider feedback networks while preserving single-cycle\\nissue of multiplies whose operands are ready.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Round 14 exposed two expensive RV32M paths. A registered product can feed\\nthe next EX result through the operand muxes, and the wide divider chains\\ntwo quotient-digit decisions per clock. The timed loop executes 93,960\\nMULs and no DIV or REM. Putting division on the same DSP used for MUL\\ncould remove both divider feedback networks while preserving single-cycle\\nissue of multiplies whose operands are ready.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use one logical 33-by-33 signed multiplier with registered input operands\\nfor all eight M operations. Gowin can map it across multiple physical DSP\\nblocks. On issue of a multiply instruction, load those registers from the\\nwrite-first ID operands and capture the signed extension bits and required\\nproduct half at the same edge. Interlock a MUL whose source still depends\\non the adjacent EX writer until MEM can supply the value. On the next\\nadvancing edge capture the selected product word in the ordinary EX/MEM\\nresult register. A consumer then gets it through the same bypass as ADD.\\nThe input registers also accept divider micro-operations during a divide.\\nThis puts operation selection before the DSP input registers and removes\\nthe separate product-half muxes from both consumer operands.\\n\\nFor DIV and REM, capture unsigned magnitudes X and D from the actual\\nforwarded EX operands. For D >= 2, prepare a conservative reciprocal.\\nLet e = max(0, floor(log2(D)) - 9), U = ceil(D / 2^e), and use a constant\\nRO\n…[4945 of 8017 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f8f2c0158933846c]…\ndelta_pct\": -2.14, \"vs_baseline\": 2258.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 88.349, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3091220, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4224, \"ff\": 1032, \"seeds\": [81.461, 88.349, 88.349], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.461, 12], [1, 88.349, 13], [2, 88.349, 13]], \"lutram\": 72, \"bsram\": 17, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_11_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/words_words_0_2_s\", \"slack_ns\": -7.276, \"arrival_ns\": 17.518, \"logic_cells\": 29, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T19:05:12.736577Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 15, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r15s1 (regression, -2.14%): Capturing MUL operands in ID stalled multiplies that needed the adjacent EX result, adding 29,425 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, while the path from EX rs2 forwarding through redirect to replay scrub control limited the shared-DSP core to a median 88.349 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
