{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if 'r8s' in x['id'] or 'r7s1' in x['id']:\n  print(x['title'],x['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Bank execute results at EX/MEM and write the register file on MEM completion {'motivation': \"At the champion's median placement, three paths are within 0.03 ns of one another.\\nThey run from the replay RAM through register reads to the fetch PC, from\\nforwarding through a multiplier to EX/MEM, and through the divider's quotient\\nrecurrence. Moving every multiply into a blocking unit added 187,665 marked cycles\\nin a scratch run. The execution pipeline needs to produce a multiply on every\\nadvancing edge.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Move result selection across the EX/MEM register. Capture the full product beside\\nthe ordinary EX/MEM result. In MEM, use registered enables to select the high\\nproduct, the low product or the ordinary result. Forward that value to the adjacent\\ninstruction and write the register file when MEM completes. Decode sees that write\\nthrough the file's write-first port. Fetch takes the array output before the\\nbypass and uses its existing operand-based predictions only when all required\\nvalues are already in the array.\\n\\nFit division to the same result boundary by splitting the radix-4 recurrence at\\ndivisor magnitude 256. Divisors from 1 through 255 need at most an eight-bit\\npartial remainder. Any divisor of 256 or more exceeds the dividend's top byte,\\nleaving only 24 quotient bits to calculate. Both paths fit the existing six RUN\\nedges. This removes the three-deep chain of full-width trial selections without\\nadding a stall to any RV32M operation.\\n\\nA scratch implementation completed ten iterations in 3,132,302 marked cycles with\\nboth bus stalls and all five expected CRCs, versus 3,122,498 for the champion.\\nGowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 68.729, 72.115 and 72.115 MHz with one\\nregistered enable per result bank. The median gives 230.23 iterations/s, 11.98%\\nabove 205.60. The acceptance threshold at this cycle count is 67.363 MHz. Gowin\\nused 4,039 logic cells, nine block RAMs and two DSPs. The scratch build passed all\\nfive cocotb suites and the selftest and three random reference trac\n…[13546 of 16618 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2236d9fb7eb1aec6]…\n.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"While held, give rs1_val and rs2_val independent enables to capture\\nthe MEM result. Preserve the consumer's other operand and metadata.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Keep the full hit check local to EX and capture its verdict in\\nEX/MEM. Inhibit divider start, branch redirect and branch training\\nduring repair. On an advancing repair edge, clear EX/MEM valid and\\nside-effect controls. This drains the load and releases its forwarding\\nselects before the held consumer executes with repaired operands.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a row, alternate two RAM pages at the same index, and delay\\nmiss responses. Check an ADD using both repaired sources, a DIVU,\\na store, a branch over a wrong-path store, and a misaligned load\\npreserving its old destination. Assert exact accepted bus transactions,\\nRVFI order and values, and load-to-ADD retirement gaps of two cycles\\non a repaired miss and one on a verified hit.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_33", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat >/srv/hwebench/tmp/19d02a47/4b8b66bd/bench-micro-lSj4CZ/variants.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nd=Path(__file__).parent\norig=Path('cores/bench/rtl')\ndef variant(name):\n    dest=d/name\n    shutil.copytree(orig,dest)\n    return dest\ndef replace(p,x,y):\n    s=p.read_text()\n    assert x in s\n    p.write_text(s.replace(x,y))\n\n# Register an unconditional load dependency and patch only on an actual miss.\nt=variant('repair')\np=t/'core.sv'\nreplace(p,'  // ── Hazard / forwarding', '''  logic load_dep1_q, load_dep2_q, repair, patch1, patch2;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (\"'!stall_id) begin\n      load_dep1_q <= rs1_match_ex;\n      load_dep2_q <= rs2_match_ex;\n    end\n  end\n  assign repair = id_ex_w.valid && ex_mem_w.ctrl.mem_read && !ex_mem_w.load_hit &&\n                  (load_dep1_q || load_dep2_q);\n  assign patch1 = repair && load_dep1_q && mem_bypass_en && !hold_mem_wb;\n  assign patch2 = repair && load_dep2_q && mem_bypass_en && !hold_mem_wb;\n\n  // ── Hazard / forwarding'\"''')\nreplace(p,'    .rs1_data (id_rs1_data),','    .patch1   (patch1),\\\\n    .patch2   (patch2),\\\\n    .patch_data(mem_bypass_data),\\\\n    .rs1_data (id_rs1_data),')\nreplace(p,'    .stall           (stall_ex_mem),','    .stall           (stall_ex_mem),\\\\n    .repair          (repair),')\nreplace(p,'.id_ex_mem_read (id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read && \"'!load_hit)'\"',\\\".id_ex_mem_read (1'b0)\\\")\nreplace(p,'.div_wait       (div_wait)', '.div_wait       (div_wait || repair)')\nreplace(p,'id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read && \"'!stall_ex_mem'\"','id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read && \"'!stall_ex_mem && !repair'\"')\np=t/'id_stage.sv'\nreplace(p,'  input  logic              flush,','  input logic patch1, patch2,\\\\n  input logic [31:0] patch_data,\\\\n  input  logic              flush,')\nreplace(p,'      reg_q.instr    <= in.instr;\\\\n    end', '''      reg