{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_73", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r11s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-001-r11s0\ntitle: Forward the producer's word index directly to the load RAM\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  In a trace of the champion's marked interval, 43,569 load-table misses\n  followed a register move at one pointer-chasing site. Two more sites\n  accounted for 42,653 misses immediately after an LW produced the base.\n  The word index for those chains can reach the RAM before the producer\n  traverses the ordinary EX bypass. The champion also puts rs1 forwarding,\n  a full address add and a tag comparison on the load-use interlock.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the load RAM a ten-bit bypass from the preceding producer. For\n  ADD or ADDI, compute the low twelve result bits from write-first\n  operands in ID and register bits 11 through 2 when the used sources\n  are ready. For an LW in EX, tap bits 11 through 2 of its raw candidate\n  word. When the younger load needs that producer and its displacement\n  is 0 through 3, use the bypass as the synchronous RAM read index.\n  This replaces the per-PC stride history with wires and an ID register.\n\n  Verify the word using two short comparisons in EX. For a ready base,\n  ID already selected the exact row with its low twelve-bit sum. Capture\n  whether carry out equals displacement sign, then compare the saved\n  base's page against the RAM page tag and check the RAM window. For a\n  dependent base, compare the ordinary EX/MEM result directly against\n  the candidate's page and registered read row, and require the low two\n  bits plus displacement to stay in that word. A stale LW candidate can\n  only select a row. Only a verified word can forward or suppress a bus\n  request. Page crossings, unsupported producers and other misses use\n  the existing interlock and the full architectural address.\n\n  A scratch implementation completed ten marked iterations in 3,061,795\n  cycles with the canonical CRCs, saving 69,286 cycles. Gowin placement\n  option 1 reached 88.308 MHz. Replacement requires a median above\n  87.47 MHz at this cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the ADD/ADDI word index and source-ready bit with ID/EX.\n      Select the raw candidate index for an LW producer. Supply the\n      selected index and its qualification to the load RAM, aligned\n      with the existing dependency matches and capture enable.\n  - file: rtl/load_predictor.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the last-address and stride-row tables with the producer\n      bypass. For a ready base capture the same-page carry test. For a\n      pending base capture eligibility and the selected row. Store data,\n      valid and an eight-bit page tag in each of the 1,024 rows. Preserve\n      the reset scrub, same-edge read/write collision and older-store veto.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Check ready-base hits against ID/EX rs1_val. For a pending base\n      qualify the ordinary result bank by its registered rs1 forwarding\n      select, row, page, RAM range and low-bit carry. Use the full\n      forwarded byte address for MEM, alignment, lane selection and RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise move-to-load and LW-to-load chains, a stale pointer word\n      followed by a stalled refill, an aliased page, a displacement that\n      crosses a word, and an adjacent multiply producing a base. Check\n      accepted reads, RVFI values and retirement gaps. Exercise the new\n      index bypass in the existing stride-specific cases and retain the\n      first-row and last-row warm-reset and older-store collision checks.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nd=yaml.safe_load(open('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r11s0.yaml')); jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(d['title'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
