{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-4200 && date -u\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Give fetch a dedicated operand path from the live instruction bus\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 250.15 iterations/s. Its reported 18.321 ns path runs\\nfrom the successor block RAM through the register file to lookup_ok_q.\\nFetch currently selects the live or replayed instruction before reading\\nrs1 and rs2 for both early branch resolution and the speculative load\\ntable. Only architectural decode needs those operands on every issue.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion scores 250.15 iterations/s. Its reported 18.321 ns path runs\\nfrom the successor block RAM through the register file to lookup_ok_q.\\nFetch currently selects the live or replayed instruction before reading\\nrs1 and rs2 for both early branch resolution and the speculative load\\ntable. Only architectural decode needs those operands on every issue.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Fork operand delivery before the instruction-source mux. Two extra\\nasynchronous register-file read ports take their addresses directly\\nfrom the live bus. When imemReady is high, fetch can use those values\\nfor its existing ready-operand BEQ/BNE and zero-offset JALR predictions.\\nWhen issuing a replayed word, fetch uses the existing branch counter\\nfor a conditional branch and lets EX resolve JALR. Architectural ID\\ncontinues to read the selected instruction through its write-first ports.\\n\\nUse the same live rs1 port to launch a data-table probe without an ID\\naddress adder. For a ready live base and a byte displacement from 0\\nthrough 3, read the base word row directly. For every other case,\\nincluding replay, read the existing PC-indexed stride row. EX checks\\nthe full forwarded effective word address, alignment and validity.\\nIf adding a small displacement crosses a word boundary, the ordinary\\nmiss path supplies the correct word.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten stalled CoreMark iterations in\\n3,175,884 marked cycles with all five canonical CRCs. At that cycle\\ncount the 4.6% acceptance margin r\n…[1158 of 4230 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:95900ad789ff1c4f]…\nwith neither writer pending. For the load probe, a\\nmatching MEM writer supplies mem_bypass_data, while an EX match or\\nan unready instruction bus selects the stride path. Pass the live\\nI-immediate to the probe. Keep issue, hazard detection, architectural\\noperands and RVFI associated with the actual selected instruction.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/load_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Select base_low[11:2] only when base_ready and i_imm[11:2] is zero.\\nOtherwise use next_row[issue_pc_index]. Store valid, address[19:12]\\nand data in each of the 1024 block-RAM rows. Capture the requested\\nten-bit row alongside the synchronous read to reconstruct the full\\ncandidate word address. Capture the concurrent MEM update enable\\nand write row on the same edge and compare the registered rows in EX.\\nHold them with the candidate through stalls. Retain the scrub gate,\\nlive older-store veto, refill rules and stride training.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise offsets 0 thr\nSun Nov 22 14:35:38 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
