{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_91","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r13s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-001-r13s0\ntitle: Advance replay RAM probes independently of the EX issue veto\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's placement-0 critical path starts at EX/MEM alu_result and ends at the clock enable of older.source in fetch. The same issue signal controls the instruction RAM read. Both structures generate hints, and IF already checks each returned word against the full fetch address. A probe can run before EX decides whether the fetched instruction may issue.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the replay enables at the existing fabric candidate register. Launch the word RAM read and advance the two-sample source history when fetch has a live or tag-matched word, the fence barrier is clear and ID can advance. A redirect or an interlocked load consumer can therefore launch a harmless extra probe. Train the row hints against that same probe history. Sample live instruction fills only from a ready bus inside the instruction window.\n  \n  Keep the fabric candidate and its collision-permission bit together until an architectural issue replaces them. This keeps the current word available when the PC holds. Register the launched read row and simultaneous fill row at the probe edge and compare those registers in the response stage, so the exception lookup and collision comparison occupy different cycles. Preserve live-bus priority, the full destination-PC match, and reset and FENCE.I invalidation of every in-flight permission. PC advance, ID/EX validity and fence issue continue to use the architectural issue rules.\n  \n  A preliminary version that advanced the candidate on every available word reached 90.023 MHz in Gowin placement 1 and completed ten iterations in 3,098,509 marked cycles with all five CRCs. Holding the candidate and splitting the read-row collision check target its cycle cost and clock margin. At the champion's 3,061,795 cycles the acceptance threshold is just over 93.53 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Give the replay read, source history and associated read metadata a local probe enable. Hold the validated fabric response on architectural stalls. Align the registered collision verdict with the word it qualifies and discard pending permissions on reset or an issued FENCE.I.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r13s0.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('validated',p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
