{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i -o '.{0,100}(one-hot|carry.select|carry.save|prefix|thermometer|permutation|result bank|early-out|radix-16|mux.*multipl).{0,150}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -60\"", "aggregated_output": "8:and the destinations of all three older potential writers.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Compute two four-way, one-hot forwarding selections during decode, one\\nper source. Compare raw fetch bits 19:15 and 24:20 with the destinations\\ncurrently in EX, MEM and WB. Reje\n8:r's effective write enable, including trap suppression. The ID/EX edge captures both youngest-first one-hot selections and one shared copy of WB data. The selections and saved data hold through stalls. EX masks and combines the four sources for both operand\n8: 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r3s0 (regression, +20.45%): Registering youngest-first one-hot forwarding selects and WB data at ID/EX moved forwarding priority off both EX operand paths at no CoreMark cycle cost, and mapping the register file \n20:ctly from the\\nforwarded registers reached 64.921 MHz on placement option 1. The\\nadjacent-producer mux still sat before the DSP. The bracketed trace\\ncontains 93,960 multiplies in 3,122,498 cycles, all MUL.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"On the champion's median Gowin placement, the 20.861 ns path from\\nrs1_match_q through EX to alu_result is within 0.010 ns of the worst\\nfetch path. A scratch change feeding the multiplier directly from the\\nforwarded registers reached 64.921 MHz on placement option 1. The\\nadjacent-producer mux still sat before the DSP. The bracketed trace\\ncontains 93,960 multiplies in 3,122,498 cycles, all MUL.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give the multiplier registered inputs. Capture the two MEM/WB-bypassed\\noperands on decode issue, with the signedness appropriate to MUL,\\nMULH, MULHSU or MULHU. The DSP can start directly from these flops.\\nA multiply with an unresolved adjacent writer takes one repair cycle\\nin EX to overwrite the same input flops with the actual forwarded\\nvalues. It then executes through the identical product path. This\\nremoves both the adjacent bypass and PC/immediate selection from the\\nDSP inputs while preserving one-cycle issue for independent multiplies.\\nMeasure repair cycles and median Fmax together. \n…[16376 of 19448 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e717f6111e939d6c]…\nn source and pass both possible direct successors into ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve branches and JALR with ordinary-only operand forwarding and select recovery from the captured direction and complete successor addresses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Hold a product-dependent control transfer for one advancing cycle, with older dmem and divide holds taking precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check both instruction sources, WB metadata freshness, x0, JALR bit-one faults and MUL-high dependencies on each branch operand under data-bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Maintain WB zero and JALR metadata, look up the live and replay source indices separately, and identify true adjacent multiply dependencies of control transfers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select narrow direction and target predictions from the appropriat\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg; cat tools/eval/gowin.py | sed -n '125,210p'; command -v gw_sh; ls -d /opt/*; ls -d /tmp/* 2>/dev/null | head\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n    }\n\n\ndef _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Run the build; True if it hit BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC (its process group is\n    killed).\"\"\"\n    import subprocess\n    with log.open(\"w\") as f:\n        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n                                stdout=f, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n                                env=env, start_new_session=True)\n        try:\n            proc.wait(timeout=BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC)\n            return False\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n         \n…[2652 of 5724 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:64917c38ae2ffb47]…\nutram\": ref[\"lutram\"],\n        \"bsram\": ref[\"bsram\"], \"dsp\": ref[\"dsp\"], \"logic_levels\": ref[\"levels\"],\n        \"critical_path\": (ref.get(\"critical_paths\") or [None])[0],\n    }\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\n    with the worst paths, for agents' own checks.\"\"\"\n    import argparse, json\n    from tools.eval.fpga import _bench_sv\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"target\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--worktree\", default=\".\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--paths\", type=int, default=5)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--all-options\", action=\"store_true\",\n                    help=\"build every placement option the evaluator uses (default: option 0 only)\")\n    a = ap.parse_args(argv)\n/opt/gowin\n/opt/hwe-python\n/opt/hwe-toolchain\n/tmp/FuuBKVNja9\n/tmp/auto-arch-tournament.formal.lock\n/tmp/bshim-t\n/tmp/cc-socks\n/tmp/claude-1000\n/tmp/claude-empty-3005YM\n/tmp/claude-empty-5J3gh3\n/tmp/claude-empty-8FqzZj\n/tmp/claude-empty-8gva93\n/tmp/claude-empty-8h1tjt\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
