{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r12s0','r12s1','r12s2','r14s0')):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-001-r12s0 {'motivation': \"On the champion's 89.419 MHz median placement the longest reported setup\\npath starts at the fetch PC selector and ends at read_ok_q. It crosses\\nthe asynchronous exception RAM, its tag check, the replay read-address\\nmux and the comparison against the concurrent fill row. The two-issue\\nlookahead gives fetch an intervening clock edge at which to select the word.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Read PC+8 and the exception entry's row concurrently from two copies\\nof the instruction-word RAM. Register the exception tag-match bit with\\nthose reads. At the next accepted issue use that bit to select which RAM\\noutput enters the existing fabric candidate register. Register the two\\nread addresses and concurrent fill metadata at the read edge and test\\nthe selected port's collision in the response stage. This removes tag\\nqualification and row selection from the RAM address setup path and moves\\ncollision checking out of that cycle.\\n\\nThis retiming should preserve the champion's 3,061,795 marked cycles.\\nAt that count the replacement threshold is just above 93.53 MHz.\\nCompare the three-placement median and the marked interval, since the\\nRF and EX paths are close to the replay path on the current placement.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Give the sequential and exception probes independent synchronous read\\nports with identical fill and scrub writes. Pipeline their select,\\nread rows, scrub eligibility and same-edge write metadata on issue.\\nHold both responses and their metadata across stalls and redirects.\\nFlush validity on reset and FENCE.I. Keep candidate selection before\\nthe fabric register, the final full-PC check and live-bus priority.\\n'}]}\nhyp-20261122-002-r12s1 {'motivation': \"The champion takes 3,061,795 cycles for ten marked iterations. On placement 0,\\nits longest path runs from the adjacent producer's result to the clock enable\\nof fetch history. On placements 1 and 2 the longest pa\n…[6417 of 9489 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:634fe368d0d9dfe0]…\nissue interval, before enabling the fabric\\ncandidate. This removes collision detection from address setup. Compare\\nboth marked cycles and median Fmax. At 3,061,795 cycles the 4.6 percent\\nreplacement margin requires more than 93.53 MHz.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Reindex the word RAM and replace the tagged exception mux with the\\nencoded row table. Advance source history and both read stages on\\naccepted issue. Carry the sampled collision metadata across holds.\\nPreserve ready-bus priority, the full in-window PC check, and reset\\nand FENCE.I scrubbing of both tables and all outstanding permissions.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise sequential replay across the modulo-1024 wrap and alternating\\nsources sharing a row-table index. Check retired PCs and words on\\ninstruction waits, including a simultaneous physical-row fill followed\\nby a hold and a code-store/FENCE.I sequence.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
