{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r9s1'):\n  print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': 'The champion scores 250.15 iterations/s. Its reported 18.321 ns path runs\\nfrom the successor block RAM through the register file to lookup_ok_q.\\nFetch currently selects the live or replayed instruction before reading\\nrs1 and rs2 for both early branch resolution and the speculative load\\ntable. Only architectural decode needs those operands on every issue.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Fork operand delivery before the instruction-source mux. Two extra\\nasynchronous register-file read ports take their addresses directly\\nfrom the live bus. When imemReady is high, fetch can use those values\\nfor its existing ready-operand BEQ/BNE and zero-offset JALR predictions.\\nWhen issuing a replayed word, fetch uses the existing branch counter\\nfor a conditional branch and lets EX resolve JALR. Architectural ID\\ncontinues to read the selected instruction through its write-first ports.\\n\\nUse the same live rs1 port to launch a data-table probe without an ID\\naddress adder. For a ready live base and a byte displacement from 0\\nthrough 3, read the base word row directly. For every other case,\\nincluding replay, read the existing PC-indexed stride row. EX checks\\nthe full forwarded effective word address, alignment and validity.\\nIf adding a small displacement crosses a word boundary, the ordinary\\nmiss path supplies the correct word.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten stalled CoreMark iterations in\\n3,175,884 marked cycles with all five canonical CRCs. At that cycle\\ncount the 4.6% acceptance margin requires more than 83.10 MHz.\\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 81.127, 85.141 and\\n85.141 MHz. The median yields 268.09 iterations/s, 7.17% above the\\nchampion. The prototype used 4,304 logic cells, 764 registers, nine\\nblock RAMs and two DSPs. Selftest and all three random RVFI traces\\nmatched the reference with ready and stalled buses. All five cocotb\\nsuites passed after four cache tests used preloaded base addresses\\nfor their first-visit hit cases. Formal verification is pending.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitne\n…[1311 of 4383 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e554df7db6ba30e6]…\nre the concurrent MEM update enable\\nand write row on the same edge and compare the registered rows in EX.\\nHold them with the candidate through stalls. Retain the scrub gate,\\nlive older-store veto, refill rules and stride training.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise offsets 0 through 3 on an aligned live base and a byte load\\ncrossing into the next word from an unaligned base. Check the accepted\\nreads, byte masks, values and adjacent consumer retirement gaps.\\nFor collision, alias and warm-reset cases that require a first-visit\\nhit on a previously filled row, put the target word address in rs1\\nand use displacement zero. Keep the same effective addresses,\\naccepted-transaction checks and retirement assertions. Warm the\\nstride path before requiring bus-free hits for negative or larger\\ndisplacements. Exercise a replayed branch, JALR and load with\\nunrelated live bus bits. Check the exact RVFI sequence and absence\\nof wrong-path stores, including under data backpressure.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
