{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r13s0','r13s2')):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261122-001-r13s0 Split the replay enables at the existing fabric candidate register. Launch the word RAM read and advance the two-sample source history when fetch has a live or tag-matched word, the fence barrier is clear and ID can advance. A redirect or an interlocked load consumer can therefore launch a harmless extra probe. Train the row hints against that same probe history. Sample live instruction fills only from a ready bus inside the instruction window.\n\nKeep the fabric candidate and its collision-permission bit together until an architectural issue replaces them. This keeps the current word available when the PC holds. Register the launched read row and simultaneous fill row at the probe edge and compare those registers in the response stage, so the exception lookup and collision comparison occupy different cycles. Preserve live-bus priority, the full destination-PC match, and reset and FENCE.I invalidation of every in-flight permission. PC advance, ID/EX validity and fence issue continue to use the architectural issue rules.\n\nA preliminary version that advanced the candidate on every available word reached 90.023 MHz in Gowin placement 1 and completed ten iterations in 3,098,509 marked cycles with all five CRCs. Holding the candidate and splitting the read-row collision check target its cycle cost and clock margin. At the champion's 3,061,795 cycles the acceptance threshold is just over 93.53 MHz.\n\nhyp-20261122-003-r13s2 For each observed sequence P, Q, R, S of accepted instruction PCs, train\none synchronous RAM entry indexed by P's word address. Store R's full\nin-window word PC, its accepted instruction, and S's in-window word PC.\nOn issue at P read the entry, then clock the response into fabric on the\nnext issue. At R a valid full-PC match supplies a successor directly from\nregisters. Use it for next-PC prediction even on a live-bus issue. A ready\nbus still supplies the architectural instruction. On a predictor miss\npredict PC+4. The same entry can supply R's instruction during a bus wait.\nThis gives one prediction table a direct PC index and removes both the\nasynchronous exception lookup and the RF comparison from fetch steering.\n\nVerify the prediction for every issued instruction. In parallel with ID,\ncompare the proposed word PC with PC+4 and with the current instruction's\ndirect target. Register both match bits and both addresses. EX selects\nthe appropriate match with the resolved direction and alignment result.\nFor a legal taken JALR compare against the full forwarded target after\nclearing bit zero. Recover to the architectural successor on any mismatch,\nincluding changed live code or an ordinary instruction predicted taken.\nThe principal tradeoff is extra recoveries where a source has multiple\npaths. Measure their cycle cost against the placement-median clock gain.\nAt the original cycle count the acceptance threshold is 93.53 MHz.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
