{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r15s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-001-r15s0\ntitle: Compare operand low bytes before fetch selects the instruction source\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's median placement has a 16.461 ns arrival from imemReady\n  through register-file selection and the BEQ/BNE comparison to alternate_pc.\n  A scratch run comparing just rs1[7:0] and rs2[7:0] in fetch reproduced all\n  3,061,795 marked cycles and the five CoreMark CRCs. This makes the equality\n  hint small enough to compute separately for the live and replay words.\nhypothesis: |\n  Maintain an eight-bit copy of each register's low byte at the existing\n  MEM write port. Address one pair of narrow reads directly from the live\n  instruction bus. Address the other pair from the instruction RAM response\n  one issue earlier, and capture its equality bit with the fabric replay\n  candidate. The instruction-source mux then selects a one-bit hint. Use\n  it for ready-operand BEQ/BNE prediction, with inversion for BNE and the\n  current counter fallback for pending writers. EX resolves the full operands\n  and corrects a byte collision or a replay hint made stale by a later write.\n  Capture the two direct successors separately so the late direction bit\n  does not drive a word-wide mux at the ID/EX edge.\n\n  Initialize the narrow copies with one shared scrub index. Architectural\n  writes have priority. On idle write slots zero each still-unwritten row,\n  including x0, and advance past rows already written since reset. Until the\n  sweep completes, use a defined cold hint. This moves the per-register\n  written-bit mask out of all four speculative read ports. Normal ID operands,\n  load probes and JALR targets retain their full precision.\n\n  A scratch version with read-side validity masks completed in 3,062,420\n  marked cycles. Moving direct successor selection behind ID reached\n  87.190 MHz on placement 1 with those masks. The proposed write-side\n  initialization targets their remaining address decode and fanout. At that\n  cycle count the three-placement median must exceed 93.55 MHz for acceptance.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: Add the low-byte mirror with two independent source pairs, write-priority initialization and a defined pre-scrub result. Keep normal write-first reads and x0 semantics.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire live indices from io_imemData and early replay indices from IF to the byte ports. Return their equality bits to fetch.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Expose the RAM response's register indices and advance its equality bit on the same enable as candidate. Select the corresponding equality hint for conditional branches and retain the existing operand-ready tests.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Form the direct recovery address from registered predicted_taken, pc_plus4 and direct_target. Resolve direction, alignment and traps using the complete architectural operands.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise BEQ and BNE with equal low bytes and unequal upper bits on live and replay fetches. Change a source between replay sampling and issue, hold the candidate through a stall, and check retired PCs and wrong-path store suppression.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r15s0.yaml')\nv=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()); jsonschema.validate(v,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(v['id'], 'schema OK')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
