uld raise the clock rate for every CoreMark instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unrolled radix-4 restoring\\ndivider inside the ALU. Each of 16 steps consumes two dividend bits and\\ncomputes three trial differences in parallel. Their borrow flags select\\nboth the next quotient digit and an already computed remainder. This\\nhalves the \n…[18496 of 21568 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:73c7ff4cd1f6153e]…\nregression\", \"fitness\": 12.91, \"delta_pct\": 6.52, \"vs_baseline\": 6.52, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.426, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4202272, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12413, \"ff\": 469, \"seeds\": [5.076, 5.426, 5.426], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.076, 145], [1, 5.426, 150], [2, 5.426, 150]], \"lutram\": 24, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -192.001, \"arrival_ns\": 202.296, \"logic_cells\": 151, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 145, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T03:01:46.196025Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +6.52%): The 128-entry bimodal predictor and fetch-time JAL targets cut CoreMark cycles by about 6.4% by avoiding one IF/ID flush per correctly predicted taken transfer, while the single-cycle EX divider still limited Fmax to about 5.4 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r1s0 (regression, +32.67%): Parallel radix-4 trials raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.44 to 7.22 MHz, but chaining 16 remainder selections in one EX cycle kept it below the multicycle divider’s 32 MHz.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r1s1 (improvement, +487.71%): Limiting the restoring divider to eight quotient steps per clock shortened the EX critical path, and its six-cycle latency cost no timed CoreMark cycles because `iterate` and its callees execute no DIV or REM instructions.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +6.52%): The 128-entry bimodal predictor and fetch-time JAL targets cut CoreMark cycles by about 6.4% by avoiding one IF/ID flush per correctly predicted taken transfer, while the single-cycle EX divider still limited Fmax to about 5.4 MHz.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
