{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"agent_message","text":"Wrote and schema-validated the [five-bit divider hypothesis](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-001-r2s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r2s0.yaml).\n\nThe prototype shortened the divider’s feedback path from eight quotient bits per clock to five. Median Gowin Fmax rose from 31.991 to **45.009 MHz**. Ten CoreMark iterations still took 4,491,485 bracketed cycles, yielding **100.21 iterations/s, 40.7% above the champion**.\n\nDIV/REM latency rose from six to nine EX cycles. The prototype passed all 53 fast formal checks, all five cocotb suites, and cosimulation on all five test binaries."}}
