{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python -c 'import json; r=[json.loads(l) for l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\") if \\\"hyp-20261122-002-r3s1\\\" in l]; print(json.dumps(r,indent=2))'\"", "aggregated_output": "[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r3s1\",\n    \"title\": \"Resolve older operand dependencies before execute\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations at 47.7 MHz. In the median Gowin placement, a register-file BSRAM output feeds EX branch resolution and returns through hazard control to an ID/EX operand register in 26.259 ns. The other read port feeds a dmem address input through forwarding and the multiplier in 26.246 ns. Both paths pay the cost of selecting EX operands before the actual computation begins.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": {\n      \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations at 47.7 MHz. In the median Gowin placement, a register-file BSRAM output feeds EX branch resolution and returns through hazard control to an ID/EX operand register in 26.259 ns. The other read port feeds a dmem address input through forwarding and the multiplier in 26.246 ns. Both paths pay the cost of selecting EX operands before the actual computation begins.\\n\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"At decode, assemble each source from the register file, the current WB write, or the result completing in MEM. Give MEM first priority and WB second. Capture that value at the existing ID/EX boundary. Only the immediately preceding producer can still supersede it. While the consumer is in ID, compare its two source addresses with the nonzero destination in ID/EX and register the two match bits beside the operands. In EX each source needs one 2:1 mux controlled by its match bit and the EX/MEM producer's trap-resolved write enable.\\n\\nUse two distributed asynchronous-read RAM replicas so each ID/EX operand flop captures a completed read. Drive speculative read addresses and match comparisons from raw imem instruction fields. Let valid and control bits squash bubbles. Hold both captured values and producer matches on backpressure. For loads, tap the existing aligned, extended MEM result and admit it only when the pipeline advances. The one-cycle load-use interl\n…[5633 of 8705 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b4d5c49737c63971]…\n\n        60.653,\n        10\n      ],\n      [\n        1,\n        62.655,\n        10\n      ],\n      [\n        2,\n        62.655,\n        10\n      ]\n    ],\n    \"lutram\": 32,\n    \"bsram\": 4,\n    \"dsp\": 6,\n    \"critical_path\": {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_25_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -11.487,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 21.782,\n      \"logic_cells\": 10,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"logic_levels\": 10,\n    \"formal_passed\": true,\n    \"cosim_passed\": true,\n    \"error\": null,\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T03:50:51.091903Z\",\n    \"slot\": 1,\n    \"round_id\": 3,\n    \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r3s1 (improvement, +31.36%): Resolving MEM and WB bypasses in ID and registering each source\\u2019s match with the adjacent producer reduced EX forwarding to one 2:1 mux per operand, raising Fmax while preserving CoreMark\\u2019s 4,491,485 timed cycles.\"\n  }\n]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
