max.\\nThe main timing risk is the routing and selection delay of the three\\nparallel differences per step.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 25, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"In the real DIV/REM datapath, form unsigned operand magnitudes and\\nprecompute D, 2D and 3D once at 34-bit precision. Start with remainder\\nzero. At step k (1 through 16), append the next two most-significant\\nunconsumed dividend bits to the remainder. This trial dividend fits\\nin 2k bits\n…[13369 of 16441 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a69541e0d27a29a7]…\ninstruction retains its match bits.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire raw fetch source addresses to the RF and match logic. Select a qualified MEM value per matching source ahead of the write-first RF outputs at the ID inputs. Keep PC, instruction metadata and load-use hazard control on their existing issue schedule.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Feed each EX operand from its captured ID value or the adjacent EX/MEM result. Use these operands for the ALU, divider launch, branches, JALR, store data and RVFI.'}, {'file': 'test/test_reg_file.py', 'description': 'Check both replicas after a warm reset and after same-address read/write collisions, including x0.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise consecutive writers to one rd followed by a two-source consumer, a dependent byte load held by dmem backpressure, and a trapping misaligned load followed by a consumer of its old rd. Check RVFI operands, result and retirement order.'}]}, 'implementation_notes': ''}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
