{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r6s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r6s0\ntitle: Register forwarded multiply operands before the DSP\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires ten CoreMark iterations in 3,394,055 cycles at\n  62.730 MHz. Its option-0 timing path starts at EX/MEM.alu_result,\n  crosses the EX ALU, and ends at data RAM. An earlier forwarding\n  experiment traced this path through the multiplier. Today every MUL\n  variant has operand forwarding, a full product, and ALU result\n  selection in the same cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give MUL, MULH, MULHU and MULHSU two EX beats. On the first beat latch\n  the forwarded register operands and operation and insert one EX/MEM\n  bubble. On the second beat compute the selected product from those\n  flops and send it directly to the EX/MEM result register. Releasing\n  decode on that edge lets an adjacent consumer use ordinary forwarding.\n  This removes the forwarding and ALU input muxes from the DSP input\n  path. A 70 MHz median with one percent more marked cycles would give\n  about 204 iterations/s. The tradeoff is one extra beat per multiply.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Capture post-forward rs1 and rs2 once for a valid multiply when EX can advance. Use a pending bit with the existing EX wait and bubble protocol. Hold the captured operation across backpressure, consume it once, cancel it on reset, and use the captured operands for RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Feed the product logic from the captured operands, implement the signed and unsigned halves with explicit widths, and expose the selected product separately from the base ALU result. Route all four ALTOPS formulas through the same two-beat timing.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Adapt multiply checks to the registered operands and verify exact high and low halves for mixed signs, extrema and changing live inputs. Retain all divider checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise adjacent producer-to-MUL and MUL-to-consumer bypasses, consecutive multiply variants, and a multiply held behind a waiting data access. Check single retirement, source values and destination data.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
