{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r6s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r6s0\ntitle: Forward an accepted RAM load from EX/MEM to its immediate consumer\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current load-use interlock inserts a bubble even when decode knows\n  the load address and the data port is idle during EX. Round 5 showed\n  that an early access could remove that bubble. On the successor-table\n  champion the relevant baseline is now 3,394,055 cycles for ten\n  iterations at 62.730 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Form the I-type effective address in ID from the MEM/WB-bypassed base\n  and register it on the data port. Issue a load in EX when its base\n  was ready in ID, the address is aligned for the access width and lies\n  in ordinary RAM, and no older access owns the port. On acceptance,\n  latch the extended value for adjacent EX forwarding. The consumer can\n  then issue on the load's acceptance edge. An unaccepted request uses\n  the existing MEM interlock and retains its address until acknowledged.\n\n  An isolated load-only prototype completed the stalled CoreMark run in\n  3,196,623 marked cycles and passed all five CRCs. Gowin placement\n  options 0, 1 and 2 reached 57.688, 62.683 and 62.683 MHz. The median\n  gives 196.09 iterations/s, about 6.1% above the champion.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the signed decode address and base readiness. On an\n      advancing EX edge, give any access moving to MEM priority for the\n      next port address. Gate early reads by validity, ownership,\n      alignment, RAM bounds and reset. A ready early read releases the\n      load-use interlock, selects its saved value for adjacent forwarding\n      and suppresses a duplicate MEM request. Keep stores and MMIO\n      ordered on the MEM path.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose the full architectural address from forwarded rs1 plus the\n      I/S immediate. Capture the early-completion bit, raw response,\n      extended value and architectural address alongside the EX/MEM load\n      under its existing hold enable.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the saved effective address for lane masks, traps and RVFI.\n      Use the saved word for an EX-completed load and the accepted bus\n      word for a MEM load. Preserve the MEM-to-ID bypass, WB data,\n      byte and halfword extension, and raw RVFI memory fields.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check one retirement cycle between an accepted early load and its\n      consumer. Deny an early request and verify its stable retry, one\n      accepted read and the fallback load-use bubble. Cover dependent\n      bases, older stores, signed subword lanes, MMIO, misalignment,\n      redirects and prolonged backpressure.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
