{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'micro_opt' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-1100 && ls cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && head -c 4500 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-29140aa\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T02:35:47.912155Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve two quotient bits per step in the combinational divider\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path runs from the MEM/WB destination\\nregister through forwarding and the EX ALU. The ALU evaluates signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. A chain of quotient-bit\\ndecisions is a plausible source of the reported 156-cell path. Shortening\\nit would raise the clock rate for every CoreMark instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path runs from the MEM/WB destination\\nregister through forwarding and the EX ALU. The ALU evaluates signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. A chain of quotient-bit\\ndecisions is a plausible source of the reported 156-cell path. Shortening\\nit would raise the clock rate for every CoreMark instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unrolled radix-4 restoring\\ndivider inside the ALU. Each of 16 steps consumes two dividend bits and\\ncomputes three trial differences in paral\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten the divider feedback path to five quotient bits per clock\", \n…[8869 of 11941 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:77eb72c9050bc99f]…\nemainder. Preserve the existing ALTOPS formulas.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise quotient-digit transitions with dividends one below, at and\\none above D, 2D and 3D wherever representable. Include large unsigned\\ndivisors with 2D or 3D above 32 bits, mixed signed operands, and\\nquotients with alternating base-4 digits. Check both quotient and\\nremainder against an integer reference that truncates toward zero.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 25, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"In the real DIV/REM datapath, form unsigned operand magnitudes and\\nprecompute D, 2D and 3D once at 34-bit precision. Start with remainder\\nzero. At step k (1 through 16), append the next two most-significant\\nunconsumed dividend bits to the remainder. This trial dividend fits\\nin 2k bits. For each divisor multiple, subtract its low 2k bits with\\nan explicit borrow output. A trial fits when its upper multiple bits\\nare zero and the subtraction has no b", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
