{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport tempfile,shutil\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nbase=Path(tempfile.gettempdir())/'prefix-divider-eegy0os4'\ndef run(kind):\n r=shutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',base/f'rtl_{kind}')\n p=r/'alu.sv'\n s=p.read_text()\n if kind\"'!='\"'oh':\n  s=s.replace('  logic [1:0] digit;', '''  logic [1:0] digit;\n  logic [34:0] n1, n2, n3;''').replace('      divisor_3x_q <= divisor_1x + divisor_2x;', \\\"\\\"\\\"      n1 <= -{3'b0,divisor_q};\n      n2 <= -{2'b0,divisor_q,1'b0};\n      n3 <= {3'b0,divisor_q} - {1'b0,divisor_q,2'b0};\\\"\\\"\\\")\n  for i,m in enumerate(('divisor_1x','divisor_2x','divisor_3x_q'),1):\n   s=s.replace('- {1\\\\'b0, '+m+'};','+ n'+str(i)+';')\n if kind\"'!='\"'neg':\n  b=s.index('      if (diff2[34])')\n  e=s.index('      quotient_next = {',b)\n  s=s[:b]+'''      remainder_next = ({32{diff1[34]}} & trial[31:0]) |\n                       ({32{\"'!diff1[34] && diff2[34]}} & diff1[31:0]) |\n                       ({32{!diff2[34] && diff3[34]}} & diff2[31:0]) |\n                       ({32{!diff3[34]}} & diff3[31:0]);\n      digit = {!diff2[34],(!diff1[34] && diff2[34]) || !diff3[34]};\n'\"'''+s[e:]\n p.write_text(s)\n print(kind,build('.',r,'fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,base/f'{kind}-timing'),flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as ex:\n list(ex.map(run,['oh','neg','negoh']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r7s0.yaml')\ns=\\\"\\\"\\\"id: hyp-20261122-001-r7s0\ntitle: Register multiply operands before the DSP and replay adjacent dependencies\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On the champion's median Gowin placement, the 20.861 ns path from\n  rs1_match_q through EX to alu_result is within 0.010 ns of the worst\n  fetch path. A scratch change feeding the multiplier directly from the\n  forwarded registers reached 64.921 MHz on placement option 1. The\n  adjacent-producer mux still sat before the DSP. The bracketed trace\n  contains 93,960 multiplies in 3,122,498 cycles, all MUL.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the multiplier registered inputs. Capture the two MEM/WB-bypassed\n  operands on decode issue, with the signedness appropriate to MUL,\n  MULH, MULHSU or MULHU. The DSP can start directly from these flops.\n  A multiply with an unresolved adjacent writer takes one repair cycle\n  in EX to overwrite the same input flops with the actual forwarded\n  values. It then executes through the identical product path. This\n  removes both the adjacent bypass and PC/immediate selection from the\n  DSP inputs while preserving one-cycle issue for independent multiplies.\n  Measure repair cycles and median Fmax together. The acceptance clock\n  is 67.15 MHz at the original cycle count and about 69.2 MHz if every\n  multiply costs one extra cycle. Fetch and divider timing are the main\n  risks to reaching that range.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture dedicated multiplier operands at the ID/EX boundary using\n      the existing bypassed ID values. Record whether either source awaits\n      a nonzero EX destination on an issued multiply. Qualify capture and\n      pending state with issue, stall, flush and reset. Route EX repair\n      values back to these same registers with priority on the repair edge.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      For a pending multiply, wait behind an older stalled memory request,\n      then sample both resolved EX sources exactly once. Hold ID/EX and\n      feed a bubble to EX/MEM on that edge as for a waiting divide. On\n      the following advance use the product and the saved source values,\n      including for RVFI. Feed the existing arithmetic wait interlock.\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Feed one signed 33-by-33 multiply from the dedicated registers.\n      Append a sign bit to both inputs for MULH, to rs1 for MULHSU,\n      and zero otherwise. Select bits 31:0 for MUL or 63:32 for a high\n      product. Use the same captured operands for the four ALTOPS formulas.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Drive the dedicated multiply operands in the existing product checks.\n      Check mixed-sign and unsigned high halves with bit 31 set and vary\n      the ordinary ALU inputs independently of the multiply inputs.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check independent back-to-back multiplies at one retirement per\n      cycle and adjacent producers of rs1, rs2 and both sources. Include\n      a stalled older load, an x0 destination and a flushed multiply.\n      Check retirement order, both RVFI source values and every product.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\nd=yaml.safe_load(s)\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(s)\nprint('validated',p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
