{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r8s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r8s0\ntitle: Verify load hits with parallel address slices in execute\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's placement-0 report starts at the registered rs1 forwarding match\n  and ends at the fetch predecessor register. A load on this path must resolve\n  its effective address and verify the cached word before an adjacent dependent\n  instruction can issue. At 3,132,302 marked cycles, the 229.00 iter/s champion\n  requires about 75.03 MHz to clear the replacement threshold at the same IPC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Test the identity base + displacement = cached byte address in parallel slices.\n  Each slice can derive its required incoming carry from the two operand bits\n  and the expected sum bit at its least significant position. Compute each\n  slice's local sum with that carry and check both the expected bits and carry\n  into the next slice. For the lowest two bits the candidate supplies no byte\n  offset, so compute their true sum and carry directly. This makes hit latency\n  depend on a short local addition and an AND reduction. The full address adder\n  still feeds the memory port in parallel. A load hit should release the existing\n  interlock on exactly the same cycles, raising fitness through Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the effective-word-address equality in load_hit with a parallel\n      slice check of the forwarded rs1 plus the sign-extended load displacement\n      against the zero-extended candidate word address. Discard carry past bit\n      31 for RV32 wraparound. Use the true two-bit offset to check alignment and\n      extract data. Retain mem_read, candidate validity and eligibility, and\n      continue sending the full effective address to MEM and the stride trainer.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
