{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r1s1','r2s1','r2s0','r4s2','r6s2','r7s1','r8s1')): print(r['id'],r.get('hypothesis',{}).get('changes',None))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r1s1 [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Implement the clocked divider with start, result-valid and consume signals. Replace all four combinational / and % paths. Handle zero divisors, INT_MIN / -1, signed truncation toward zero and the dividend sign for REM. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS use the existing four formulas on captured operands with the same control sequence and latency.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Launch only a valid decoded divide on an advancing cycle. Save post-forward rs1 and rs2 for the retiring instruction. Hold EX/MEM on dmem backpressure, otherwise clear its entire payload on divider wait cycles so older stores, loads and register writes drain once. On completion emit the held instruction and result together. Reset clears pending work.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the EX divide interlock to hazard control. Keep the existing MEM and WB advance and forwarding paths available while the divider runs.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Hold the PC and ID/EX during divide issue and iteration. Preserve priority for an outstanding dmem stall and release the front end on the cycle the divide result enters EX/MEM.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Drive the new divider handshake for every existing DIV and REM vector. Check bounded completion, result stability until consumption, signed and unsigned edge cases, and consecutive requests. Keep the single-cycle tests for ALU and multiply operations.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a load feeding a divide under dmem backpressure, back-to-back dependent divide and remainder instructions, and an immediate result consumer. Check architectural results, forwarded RVFI operands, and exactly one ordered retirement per instruction.\\n'}]\nhyp-20261122-001-r2s0 [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Widen the combined dividend/quotient shift register to 35 bits. At issue\\nload three zero bits followed by the unsigned magnitude. Each step takes\n…[12218 of 15290 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a2684066f21cd880]…\nge.sv', 'description': \"Beside the result registers, form each source's three selects from its\\nmatch, producer write permission and MUL class. Register all six selects\\non the same edge as the consumer operands and hold them on stalls. Feed\\nthe ordinary operand mux directly from reg_q.alu_result and the ID/EX\\nsource latch. Feed the product mux from product_high and product_low.\\nUse the resulting operand pair everywhere EX consumes forwarded sources,\\nincluding stores, cached-load verification, multiplier inputs and divide\\nlaunch. A missed or misaligned adjacent load retains its existing\\ninterlock, and a faulting JAL/JALR selects the previously captured value.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise consecutive MUL and high-half multiply producers with rs1-only,\\nrs2-only and both-source dependencies. Include a dmem hold while the\\nselected product is live. Check exact operands, results and retirement\\ncycles across transitions back to an ordinary writer and a faulting link.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
