{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r9s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r9s0\ntitle: Retime the load-table collision check across the RAM read\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's reported 18.321 ns setup path starts at the instruction\n  successor RAM, passes through the register file and ends at lookup_ok_q.\n  A ready-base lookup must select rs1, add the immediate, choose the read\n  row and compare it with the concurrent write row before that edge.\n  EX already spends the following cycle verifying the candidate.\nhypothesis: |\n  Capture the physical read row alongside the synchronous load-table read.\n  On that same enable, capture the write row, whether an update fired,\n  and whether initialization had completed. In EX compare the two saved\n  row numbers in parallel with the existing full effective-address check.\n  A same-edge read/write collision always vetoes the candidate, even if\n  the block RAM returns arbitrary data. Keep the separate veto for an\n  older store currently in MEM.\n\n  The low ten word-address bits in each stored tag duplicate the physical\n  row. Supply those bits from the captured read row and store only the\n  upper eight tag bits, valid bit and 32-bit data in each entry. This\n  moves the final equality reduction off the IF-to-ID/EX timing path\n  while preserving the exact hits, misses and adjacent load forwarding.\n  At the champion's 3,132,302 marked cycles, a median above 81.97 MHz\n  would clear the tournament threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/load_predictor.sv\n    description: |\n      Infer a 1024 by 41 synchronous word table. Register read_row and\n      the same-edge update metadata whenever candidate is captured,\n      including on bubbles. Hold them together across stalls. Rebuild\n      candidate.word_addr from the stored high tag and captured row.\n      Gate eligible with the delayed collision result, scrub completion\n      at capture and the live MEM store check. Reset eligibility until\n      the first safe lookup.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
