{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_131", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r10s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-002-r10s1\ntitle: Register execute corrections at the issue boundary\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  In a reproduction of the champion's 85.513 MHz median placement, the longest path runs from the registered multiplier through rs1 forwarding, the load-address carry chain and tag comparison to an ID/EX control bit. Placement 0 ends a similar path at the fetch replay RAM. Both exist because decode waits for EX to decide whether a younger instruction may enter ID/EX. The load and its consumer still occupy separate pipeline stages on the following cycle, when the machine has a registered hit verdict.\nhypothesis: |\n  Admit the younger instruction to ID/EX on the normal advancing edge. Capture one bit per operand marking a match to the older load's nonzero destination. On a verified hit, the consumer executes immediately through the ordinary adjacent bypass. On a miss with a matching operand, hold that consumer until MEM completes the load. On the completion edge, replace each matching operand with the extended load value, clear its forwarding selects and send a bubble to EX/MEM. A trapping load preserves the captured register values. The consumer then executes exactly once. Suppress its branch recovery, predictor training, divide launch, memory requests and retirement throughout repair.\n  \n  Use the same registered issue boundary for branch correction. Decode captures control alongside a valid bit that can annul the wrong-path instruction. Fetch can clock its normal lookahead while EX registers a recovery choice. Capture the direct alternate PC and the JALR sum into separate registers while no recovery is pending. A registered redirect selects the correct bank for the very next fetch and holds it through fetch stalls. Compute jump-link write permission from jump-target alignment so a conditional branch comparison cannot delay forwarding selection. A replay still requires a valid full-PC match. Only a surviving FENCE.I may invalidate the replay state, discard pending fills and serialize fresh fetch behind an older store.\n  \n  The scratch prototype completed ten marked iterations in 3,141,587 cycles with all five CRCs and the validation banner. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 87.327, 89.532 and 89.532 MHz. The median gives 284.99 iterations/s, about 4.35 percent above the champion. Acceptance at that cycle count requires more than 89.747 MHz. Selftest and three random programs matched the reference retirement trace with both ready and stalled buses.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Capture adjacent load dependencies at issue, derive repair from the registered MEM verdict, preserve the consumer across waits and route the completing MEM value to both operand patch ports.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Replace the combinational EX load-hit interlock with a hold for the registered dependent miss. Allow the older memory operation to complete during the hold.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Separate control capture from the valid bit that kills a wrong-path packet. On the repair edge update only the matching operands of the held instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Emit a bubble during repair and clear stale forwarding selects on completion. Separate jump-link write permission from the branch comparator and deliver the full JALR word target to the recovery registers.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Register recovery selection separately from ordinary fetch advancement, bank the direct and indirect recovery PCs, and perform FENCE.I invalidation on the surviving fence in EX.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check hit and miss consumers, both sources matching, a trapping misaligned load, and a stalled load feeding a branch or divide. Check redirect through an imem wait and a killed FENCE.I alongside the existing code-store fence tests.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nprint(89.532e7/3141587, 100*(89.532e7/3141587/273.11-1))\nPY\ndate -u\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
