{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_163","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r10s1.yaml')\ns=p.read_text().replace('  \\\\n','\\\\n')\na=s.index('  Use the same registered issue');b=s.index('expected_impact:',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''  Register the recovery PC separately from ordinary fetch advancement. Capture the alternate target while no recovery is outstanding. A registered redirect selects the corrected PC on the next cycle and keeps it stable through fetch waits. Qualify link forwarding with jump alignment. Clock the physical instruction replay RAM every cycle. A delayed accepted-issue bit identifies the response to keep in a holding register if issue pauses. Advance candidate validity, collision metadata and two-issue history only on accepted correct-path issues. Only a surviving FENCE.I may invalidate replay state and serialize fresh fetch behind an older store.\n\n  A scratch prototype targets the champion's 3,131,081-cycle marker interval. Gowin placement 1 reached 88.975 MHz. At that cycle count 89.447 MHz is needed for replacement. The remaining margin depends on the placement median and the implementation of the registered correction paths.\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('deliver the full JALR word target to the recovery registers.','deliver the resolved target to the recovery register.').replace('bank the direct and indirect recovery PCs, and perform FENCE.I invalidation on the surviving fence in EX.', 'hold the corrected PC through stalls, and stage free-running replay RAM responses against accepted issue history. Invalidate on the surviving fence in EX.').replace('Check redirect through an imem wait and a killed FENCE.I alongside the existing code-store fence tests.', 'Check redirect through an imem wait and a killed FENCE.I. The load-to-branch trace should hold the successor PC during repair since the branch has already entered ID/EX. Check all retired values and wrong-path store suppression.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import parse_reports\nimport os,json\nd=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR'])/'r10s1.XAOKHW'\nfor n in ['link_probe','commit_hist','commit_fill','commit_train','commit_pc','commit_data']:\n p=d/f'{n}_sim.jsonl'\n if p.exists() and p.read_text():\n  j=json.loads(p.read_text().splitlines()[-1]);print(n,j['bench_stop_cycle']-j['bench_start_cycle'],parse_reports(d/f'{n}_p1')['fmax_mhz'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
