{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"):\n a=json.loads(s)\n if a.get(\\\"round_id\\\") in [10,8] or \\\"r10\\\" in a[\\\"id\\\"]:\n  print(a[\\\"id\\\"],a[\\\"hypothesis\\\"])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-001-r8s0 {'motivation': 'The champion selects among the ordinary EX/MEM result and two registered\\nproduct halves before forwarding either source operand. This puts the product\\nselector on dependent integer operations, branch resolution and load address\\nverification. CoreMark executes 93,960 multiplies in ten timed iterations,\\nbut only a fraction have a consumer that needs the product on the next cycle.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Drive the adjacent EX bypass from the registered ordinary result alone. Keep\\nthe full product advancing beside it and select the architectural result in\\nMEM for writeback. If a valid multiply in EX names either source field of\\nthe instruction in ID, reuse the load-use interlock for one cycle. ID then\\ncaptures the product from the register file's write-first port as MEM\\ncompletes. Independent multiplies can still issue on consecutive cycles.\\nThis trades occasional dependency bubbles for a shorter path on every\\nordinarily forwarded operand, including the load base and branch operands.\\nA multiply that consumes an adjacent ordinary ALU result still gets that\\noperand on time through the direct bypass.\\n\\nA scratch implementation completed ten iterations in 3,167,223 marked cycles,\\nup 1.11% from 3,132,302. With both bus stalls enabled it produced all five\\ncanonical CRCs and the validation message. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and\\n2 reached 73.720, 76.884 and 76.884 MHz. The median gives 242.75 iterations\\nper second, 6.00% above the champion and above the 239.53 acceptance cutoff.\\nPlacement 0 used 4,001 logic cells, 739 registers and two DSPs. The scratch\\ncore passed all five cocotb suites with the revised timing expectations\\nand matched the reference on selftest and all three random traces with\\nready and stalled buses. All four ALTOPS multiply checks, single-channel\\nretirement uniqueness and liveness passed.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Expose a 32-bit fast_bypass outpu\n…[18986 of 22058 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7311e4d0d5098b11]…\nValidate at EX/MEM and use that result for MEM and repair. Expose the registered forwarding-source matches, and suppress the held consumer's control transfer, divider start, training and EX/MEM side effects on repair.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Replace the EX load-use address check with the registered-stage miss repair interlock. Let the older load complete while fetch and ID/EX hold the consumer.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"On repair completion, patch only source operands matching a legal nonzero load destination. Preserve the consumer's PC, instruction, other operand and retirement metadata.\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check irregular pointer and ADD-to-load sequences, including a byte offset crossing a word boundary, an incorrect producing LW candidate, and a stalled retry feeding a branch or store. Assert full RVFI, bus transactions and one-cycle forwarding on hits. Keep the stride-alias test on a producer ineligible for the new hint.'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
