{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith('r7s2'): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'], d['changes'],d['critical_path'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith('r7s2'): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'], d['changes'],d['critical_path'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Predict the next PC from a 128-entry tagged branch target buffer and the\nexisting two-bit direction counters. Use that address both to advance\nfetch and to launch a synchronous read of a 1,024-word instruction RAM.\nA single fill at a destination PC then serves sequential, taken and\nrecovery paths to that instruction. The predicted address is available\nwithout waiting for decode to read branch operands.\n\nSplit the instruction field instr[31:15] from the block RAM row. It\ncontains both RF addresses and the I-immediate used to predict a load\nrow. Give these 17 bits a distributed RAM with an asynchronous read at\nthe predicted next index and a capture flop on the same edge as the\nblock RAM read. Reassemble the saved instruction in decode. This makes\nthe saved operand fields available at flop clock-to-Q and keeps the\ndata-RAM address calculation out of the instruction block RAM output path.\n\nA prototype with the entire instruction in block RAM completed ten\niterations in 3,104,776 marked\ncycles with both bus stalls, the five expected CRCs and the validation\nbanner. Gowin measured 62.193, 65.910 and 65.910 MHz, yielding 212.29\niterations/s. That is 3.25% above 205.60. At that cycle count, the\n4.6% replacement margin requires more than 66.77 MHz. Its median\nplacement had a path from the instruction block RAM through the\nload predictor to lookup_ok_q. The proposed split targets that path.\nThe split layout has not been timed. A 67.5 MHz median at the same\ncycle count would yield 217.4 iterations/s.\n [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Use PC[8:2] to read a distributed-RAM entry holding a valid bit,\\nPC[19:9], a conditional bit and an aligned target[19:2]. Train from\\nadvancing legal control transfers. Qualify both source and target\\nfor the 1 MiB window and the target for word alignment. Predict\\ntaken on a tag hit for an unconditional jump or a taken direction\\ncounter. Otherwise select PC+4. Scrub targets after reset.\\n\\nFill the instruction RAM from a ready, issued bus word. Each row\\nstores validity, PC[19:12]\n…[1182 of 4254 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6babd3b21d607265]…\n against its full forwarded target after bit\\nzero is cleared. Check stale predictions on newly fetched noncontrol\\nwords as well. Redirect to the architectural target or fallthrough,\\npreserve trap and link semantics, and train once per EX advance.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Route EX target training and recovery to fetch. Preserve redirect\\npriority and the existing issue, stall and side-effect qualification.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Train two predecessors reaching the same instruction, then hold the\\ninstruction bus low at that destination. Exercise BTB aliasing, a\\nJALR that stays taken while its target changes, a same-row fill/read\\ncollision, and code replacement across FENCE.I. Check fetch cycles,\\nthe exact RVFI instruction/PC/order trace and accepted stores.\\n'}] {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_34_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_13_s0', 'slack_ns': -10.965, 'arrival_ns': 21.259, 'logic_cells': 105, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cd \"$TMPDIR\"/benchstruct.Ki2472\ncat > split.py <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nsroot=Path('base_rtl')\ns=(sroot/'if_stage.sv').read_text()\na=s.index('  logic [31:2] pc_word;')\nb=s.index('  // Opcode bit 3',a)\nc=s.index('  assign direct_taken',b)\nd=s.index('  assign out.pc ',c)\ns=s[:a]+'''  logic [31:2] fetch_pc, held_pc, predicted_target, held_target, next_pc;\n  logic held_taken, slot_valid, have_bus, read_ok, fence_in_ex;\n  logic [31:0] pc, pc_plus4, direct_target, direct_offset;\n  logic [31:0] instr, bus_word, ram_word;\n  logic [10:0] scrub;\n  logic [9:0] wr_idx;\n  logic fill_q;\n  logic [19:2] fill_addr;\n  logic [31:0] fill_data;\n  typedef struct packed {\n    logic valid;\n    logic [19:12] tag;\n    logic [31:0] data;\n  } ic_line_t;\n  (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"block_ram\\\" *) ic_line_t ic [0:1023];\n  ic_line_t cached;\n  typedef struct packed {\n    logic valid;\n    logic unconditional;\n    logic [19:9] tag;\n    logic [19:2] target;\n  } btb_t;\n  (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"distributed_ram\\\" *) btb_t btb [0:127];\n  (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"distributed_ram\\\" *) logic [1:0] counters [0:127];\n  btb_t b;\n  logic [1:0] counter, held_counter;\n  logic pred_taken, hit, fence_issue, retry, advance, train_target_valid;\n  logic [6:0] wr_btb;\n  assign wr_idx = scrub[10] ? fill_addr[11:2] : scrub[9:0];\n  assign wr_btb = scrub[10] ? train_index : scrub[6:0];\n  assign train_target_valid = train_pc[31:20] == 0 && train_dest[31:20] == 0 && train_dest[1:0] == 0;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (\"'!scrub[10] || fill_q)\n      ic[wr_idx] <= {scrub[10], fill_addr[19:12], fill_data};\n    if (!scrub[10] || train_ctrl)\n      btb[wr_btb] <= {scrub[10] && train_target_valid, train_jump, train_pc[19:9], train_dest[19:2]};\n    if (!scrub[10] || train)\n      counters[wr_btb] <= scrub[10] ? train_counter : 2'\"'b01;\n  end\n  assign b = btb[fetch_pc[8:2]];\n  assign counter = counters[fetch_pc[8:2]];\n  assign pred_taken = scrub[10] && b.valid && fetch_pc[31:20] == 0 &&\n                      b.tag == fetch_pc[19:9] && (b.unconditional || counter[1]);\n  assign predicted_target = {12'b0, b.target};\n  assign next_pc = pred_taken ? predicted_target : (fetch_pc + 30'd1);\n  assign hit = read_ok && cached.valid && held_pc[31:20] == 0 && held_pc[19:12] == cached.tag;\n  assign instr = have_bus ? bus_word : cached.data;\n  assign fence_issue = issue && instr[6:0] == 7'b0001111 && instr[14:12] == 3'b001;\n  assign retry = slot_valid && \"'!have_bus && !hit;\n  assign advance = !(slot_valid && stall && out.valid) && !fence_in_ex;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset || fence_issue) begin\n      scrub <= 0;\n      fill_q <= 0;\n    end else begin\n      if (!scrub[10]) scrub <= scrub + 11'\"'d1;\n      fill_q <= advance && \"'!redirect && !retry && scrub[10] && imem_ready && fetch_pc[31:20] == 0;\n    end\n    fill_addr <= fetch_pc[19:2];\n    fill_data <= imem_data;\n    if (reset) fence_in_ex <= 0;\n    else if (!stall_id) fence_in_ex <= fence_issue;\n  end\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      slot_valid <= 0;\n      fetch_pc <= 0;\n    end else if (redirect) begin\n      slot_valid <= 0;\n      fetch_pc <= redirect_target;\n    end else if (fence_issue) begin\n      slot_valid <= 0;\n      fetch_pc <= held_pc + 30'\"'d1;\n    end else if (retry) begin\n      slot_valid <= 0;\n      fetch_pc <= held_pc;\n    end else if (advance) begin\n      slot_valid <= 1;\n      fetch_pc <= next_pc;\n    end\n    if (advance) begin\n      held_pc <= fetch_pc;\n      held_target <= predicted_target;\n      held_taken <= pred_taken;\n      held_counter <= counter;\n      have_bus <= imem_ready;\n      bus_word <= imem_data;\n      cached <= ic[fetch_pc[11:2]];\n      read_ok <= scrub[10] && \"'!(fill_q && wr_idx == fetch_pc[11:2]);\n    end\n  end\n  assign imem_addr = {fetch_pc, 2'\"'b00};\n  assign pc = {held_pc,2'b00};\n\n'''+s[b:c]+s[d:]\ns=s.replace('direct_taken ? pc_plus4[31:2] : direct_target[31:2]', 'held_target').replace('out.counter         = counter','out.counter         = held_counter').replace('direct_taken || jalr_taken','held_taken').replace('(imem_ready || hit) && \"'!fence_in_ex'\"','slot_valid && (have_bus || hit) && \"'!fence_in_ex'\"')\ns=s.replace('  input  logic        train,', '''  input  logic        train_ctrl, train_jump,\n  input  logic [31:0] train_pc, train_dest,\n  input  logic        train,''')\nfor j in [9,10,11]:\n name='v'+str(j)\n out=Path(name)\n shutil.copytree(sroot,out)\n t=s\n e=(sroot/'ex_stage.sv').read_text().replace('  output logic               train,','  output logic [31:0] train_dest,\\\\n  output logic               train,')\n e=e.replace('  assign train =','  assign train_dest = target;\\\\n  assign train =')\n e=e.replace('(in.predicted_taken \"'!= actual_taken)'\"','((in.predicted_taken \"'!= actual_taken) || (actual_taken && in.predicted_taken && in.alternate_pc != target[31:2]))'\"').replace('in.ctrl.is_jalr ? jalr_sum[31:2] : in.alternate_pc','actual_taken ? target[31:2] : in.pc_plus4[31:2]')\n co=(sroot/'core.sv').read_text().replace('  if_stage u_if', '  logic [31:0] train_dest;\\\\n  if_stage u_if')\n co=co.replace('    .train_index','    .train_ctrl(id_ex_w.valid && \"'!stall_ex_mem && (id_ex_w.ctrl.is_jump || id_ex_w.ctrl.is_branch)),'\"\\\\n    .train_jump(id_ex_w.ctrl.is_jump),\\\\n    .train_pc(id_ex_w.pc),\\\\n    .train_dest(train_dest),\\\\n    .train_index')\n co=co.replace('    .div_wait        (div_wait),\\\\n    .redirect', '    .div_wait        (div_wait),\\\\n    .train_dest(train_dest),\\\\n    .redirect')\n if j==10:\n  # Simplify held data gating by using skid only when valid, while keeping observable semantics.\n  # Register recovery early in ID for wrong sequential predictions on direct JAL/branch targets.\n  # Use separate registers for sequential and target, with direction bit controlling output.\n  t=t.replace('  assign next_pc = pred_taken ? predicted_target : (fetch_pc + 30\\\\'d1);', '''  logic fast_taken;\n  logic [31:2] slow_pc;\n  logic [19:2] fast_pc;\n  assign fetch_pc = fast_taken ? {12'b0, fast_pc} : slow_pc;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (advance) fast_pc <= b.target;\n    if (reset || redirect || fence_issue || retry) fast_taken <= 0;\n    else if (advance) fast_taken <= pred_taken;\n  end\n  assign next_pc = fetch_pc + 30'd1;''').replace('fetch_pc <= ', 'slow_pc <= ')\n if j==11:\n  # Direct taken target precomparison in ID shortens the recovery control path.\n  e=e.replace('in.alternate_pc \"'!= target[31:2]'\"','(in.ctrl.is_jalr ? (in.alternate_pc \"'!= target[31:2]) : !in.direct_match)'\"')\n  p=(sroot/'core_pkg.sv').read_text().replace('    logic [31:0] rs1_val;\\\\n', '    logic direct_match;\\\\n    logic [31:0] rs1_val;\\\\n',1)\n  (out/'core_pkg.sv').write_text(p)\n  i=(sroot/'id_stage.sv').read_text().replace('reg_q.alternate_pc <= in.alternate_pc;', 'reg_q.alternate_pc <= in.alternate_pc;\\\\n      reg_q.direct_match <= in.alternate_pc == in.direct_target[31:2];')\n  (out/'id_stage.sv').write_text(i)\n (out/'core.sv').write_text(co)\n (out/'ex_stage.sv').write_text(e)\n (out/'if_stage.sv').write_text(t)\nPY\npython split.py\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
