{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"):\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r10s1\\\",\\\"r11s1\\\",\\\"r12s0\\\",\\\"r12s1\\\",\\\"r12s2\\\")):\n  print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"], \\\"PATH\\\",str(r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"\\\"))[:6300], \\\"NUMBERS\\\",r[\\\"cycles\\\"],r[\\\"perturbations\\\"])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r10s1 {'motivation': \"In a reproduction of the champion's 85.513 MHz median placement, the longest path runs from the registered multiplier through rs1 forwarding, the load-address carry chain and tag comparison to an ID/EX control bit. Placement 0 ends a similar path at the fetch replay RAM. Both exist because decode waits for EX to decide whether a younger instruction may enter ID/EX. The load and its consumer still occupy separate pipeline stages on the following cycle, when the machine has a registered hit verdict.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Admit the younger instruction to ID/EX on the normal advancing edge. Capture one bit per operand marking a match to the older load's nonzero destination. On a verified hit, the consumer executes immediately through the ordinary adjacent bypass. On a miss with a matching operand, hold that consumer until MEM completes the load. On the completion edge, replace each matching operand with the extended load value, clear its forwarding selects and send a bubble to EX/MEM. A trapping load preserves the captured register values. The consumer then executes exactly once. Suppress its branch recovery, predictor training, divide launch, memory requests and retirement throughout repair.\\n\\nRegister the recovery PC separately from ordinary fetch advancement. Capture the alternate target while no recovery is outstanding. A registered redirect selects the corrected PC on the next cycle and keeps it stable through fetch waits. Qualify link forwarding with jump alignment. Clock the physical instruction replay RAM every cycle. A delayed accepted-issue bit identifies the response to keep in a holding register if issue pauses. Advance candidate validity, collision metadata and two-issue history only on accepted correct-path issues. Only a surviving FENCE.I may invalidate replay state and serialize fresh fetch behind an older store.\\n\\nA scratch prototype targets the champion's 3,131,081-cycle marker interval. Gowin placement 1 reached 88.975 MHz. At that cycle count 89.447 MHz is nee\n…[13109 of 16181 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2c5493c6b35c5180]…\nscription': 'Replace the serial exception lookup with parallel synchronous reads\\nof the rotated sequential bank and a source-indexed exception word\\nbank. Carry source tags and per-bank collision metadata to response\\nselection. Preserve issue-qualified history, live-bus priority, full\\ndestination verification, and the existing FENCE.I serialization.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a sequential second successor across row wraparound and a\\nnonsequential second successor with the same source index under\\nalternating bus waits. Test same-edge fills to each bank and a code\\npatch followed by FENCE.I. Check retired PCs and instruction words,\\nwrong-path store suppression, and replay from each warmed bank.\\n'}]} PATH {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/rs1_high_q_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/exceptions_exceptions_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -6.964, 'arrival_ns': 17.206, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu']} NUMBERS 3060918 [[0, 83.584, 12], [1, 86.455, 12], [2, 86.455, 12]]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
