{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_66", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(\\\"r3s0\\\"):print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': \"The champion reaches 47.7 MHz and runs ten CoreMark iterations in\\n4,491,485 cycles. Its median Gowin placement shows two nearly equal\\noperand paths. One feeds a branch and the fetch interlock at 26.259 ns.\\nThe other feeds the multiplier and the data-memory address at 26.246 ns.\\nBoth pay for register-file write-through and EX forwarding before their\\nresults can be used. Decode already has the consumer's source numbers\\nand the destinations of all three older potential writers.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Compute two four-way, one-hot forwarding selections during decode, one\\nper source. Compare raw fetch bits 19:15 and 24:20 with the destinations\\ncurrently in EX, MEM and WB. Reject x0 and qualify each match with the\\nproducer's effective write enable. Resolve overlapping matches youngest\\nfirst. At the ID/EX edge, register the selections and a single shared\\ncopy of current WB data alongside the instruction's register-file reads.\\n\\nIn the consumer's EX cycle the four inputs, in priority order, are the\\nEX/MEM result, MEM/WB writeback data, the saved decode-cycle WB data and\\nthe saved register-file operand. Mask each input with its registered\\nselect bit and OR the four words. The third input covers writes colliding\\nwith a register-file read in ID. This moves the write-through choice\\nand forwarding priority off both the branch and multiply operand paths.\\n\\nAn isolated prototype reached 53.428, 54.573 and 54.573 MHz in the three\\nGowin placement options. CoreMark validated all five CRCs in 4,491,485\\nmarker-to-marker cycles. The median gives 121.50 iterations/s, 14.4%\\nabove 106.20. All 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks passed. Keeping\\nthe selector in core.sv matters for Gowin mapping. Moving the same logic\\ninto a separate forwarding module measured 48.021 MHz median.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 14, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Replace the forward_unit instance with the registered selector here.\\nFor each raw fetch source form hits E, M and W against id_ex_w.rd,\\nex_mem_w.rd and wb_w_addr. Each hit requires a nonzero destination\\nand the corresponding EX write intent, MEM write intent or wb_w_en.\\nOn !stall_id register the four bits {E, !E && M, !E && !M && W,\\n!E && !M && !W}. On the same enable capture wb_w_data in a shared\\n32-bit register. These registers hold through dmem and divide stalls.\\nA flush may discard the consumer. The next accepted instruction gets\\nfresh selections. Instantiate the register file in raw-read mode.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'description': 'Remove the superseded EX-stage forwarding module. The new decode\\ncomparators and select flip-flops reside together in core.sv.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/reg_file.sv', 'description': 'Add a default-on write-first bypass parameter. With it disabled,\\nboth reads return stored data with the existing x0 behavior. The\\nintegrated core implements same-edge write-through via the saved WB\\nsource. Preserve synchronous reset and standalone write-first tests.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export ctrl_with_trap.reg_write as the write intent of the instruction\\nabout to enter EX/MEM, so a misaligned jump cannot win a match. Use\\neach four-bit mask to select the forwarded rs value for arithmetic,\\nbranches, stores, divide issue and RVFI.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export ctrl_with_trap.reg_write for the instruction about to enter\\nMEM/WB. A trapping load must allow an older matching writer to win.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Remove the deleted module from the source list. Exercise three\\nconsecutive writes to one rd followed by a consumer of both sources.\\nAlso cover a WB write colliding with decode, a consumer held behind\\na stalled store, and misaligned JAL and load instructions shadowing\\nan older write. Check retired operands and results while retaining\\nthe existing divide and load-use cycle checks.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
