{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(s)\n if r['round_id']==10 and r['slot']==1: print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\nsed -n '180,225p' cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncat cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\"","aggregated_output":"Admit the younger instruction to ID/EX on the normal advancing edge. Capture one bit per operand marking a match to the older load's nonzero destination. On a verified hit, the consumer executes immediately through the ordinary adjacent bypass. On a miss with a matching operand, hold that consumer until MEM completes the load. On the completion edge, replace each matching operand with the extended load value, clear its forwarding selects and send a bubble to EX/MEM. A trapping load preserves the captured register values. The consumer then executes exactly once. Suppress its branch recovery, predictor training, divide launch, memory requests and retirement throughout repair.\n\nRegister the recovery PC separately from ordinary fetch advancement. Capture the alternate target while no recovery is outstanding. A registered redirect selects the corrected PC on the next cycle and keeps it stable through fetch waits. Qualify link forwarding with jump alignment. Clock the physical instruction replay RAM every cycle. A delayed accepted-issue bit identifies the response to keep in a holding register if issue pauses. Advance candidate validity, collision metadata and two-issue history only on accepted correct-path issues. Only a surviving FENCE.I may invalidate replay state and serialize fresh fetch behind an older store.\n\nA scratch prototype targets the champion's 3,131,081-cycle marker interval. Gowin placement 1 reached 88.975 MHz. At that cycle count 89.447 MHz is needed for replacement. The remaining margin depends on the placement median and the implementation of the registered correction paths.\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      direct_q   <= 1'b0;\n      other_pc_q <= '0;\n    end else if (redirect) begin\n      direct_q   <= 1'b0;\n      other_pc_q <= redirect_target;\n    end else if (!stall) begin\n      direct_q   <= direct_taken;\n      other_pc_q <= jalr_taken ? {12'b0, rs1_data[19:2]} : pc_plus4[31:2];\n    end\n    if (!stall) direct_pc_q <= direct_target[19:2];\n  end\n\n  assign imem_addr           = pc;\n  assign out.pc              = pc;\n  assign out.pc_plus4        = pc_plus4;\n  assign out.direct_target   = direct_target;\n  assign out.alternate_pc    = direct_taken ? pc_plus4[31:2] : direct_target[31:2];\n  assign out.counter         = counter;\n  assign out.predicted_taken = direct_taken || jalr_taken;\n  assign out.instr           = instr;\n  assign out.valid           = (imem_ready || hit) && !fence_in_ex;\nendmodule\n// Hold the pipeline behind a waiting memory operation or divide. A\n// load-use interlock holds the PC and inserts a single bubble into EX.\nmodule hazard_unit (\n  input  logic       id_ex_mem_read,\n  input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rd,\n  input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs1,\n  input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs2,\n  input  logic       redirect,\n  input  logic       fetch_valid,\n  input  logic       dmem_ready,\n  input  logic       ex_mem_mem_op,\n  input  logic       div_wait,\n  output logic       stall_if,\n  output logic       stall_id,\n  output logic       flush_id,\n  output logic       stall_ex_mem,\n  output logic       hold_mem_wb\n);\n  logic load_use_hazard;\n\n  assign load_use_hazard = fetch_valid && id_ex_mem_read && id_ex_rd != 0 &&\n                           (id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1 || id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2);\n  assign stall_ex_mem = ex_mem_mem_op && !dmem_ready;\n  assign hold_mem_wb  = stall_ex_mem;\n  assign stall_id     = stall_ex_mem || div_wait;\n  assign stall_if     = stall_id || load_use_hazard || !fetch_valid;\n  assign flush_id     = redirect || load_use_hazard;\nendmodule\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
