gh the ordinary result register.\n      Forward that single result to adjacent consumers. Launch a divide\n      once from resolved operands and preserve both captured values for RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect accepted ID operands and product mode to the DSP input\n      registers. Interlock only a validated multiply with a matching nonzero\n      adjacent writer. A waiting consumer holds fetch and bubbles ID/EX\n      while its producer advances, subject to older memory backpressure.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Check all M operations, including reciprocal bucket transitions,\n      magnitudes 0 and 1, unsigned maxima, and dividends one either side\n      of an exact multiple. Exercise reset and held results in each phase.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check dependent and independent multiplies, signed-high variants,\n      MUL to DIV and DIV to MUL transfers, and a held MEM transaction.\n      Verify exact values, expected interlock cycles and gap-free RVFI order.\nYAML\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r15s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()); jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']==p.stem and d['category']=='structural' and type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Valid', d['title'],292.05*1.046*3091220/1e7)\nPY\ngit status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "Valid Fold RV32M execution into one registered DSP multiplier 94.4319177846\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
