s T through.\\n\\nInitialize a 36-bit quotient shift register with four leading zeros and the 32-bit dividend magnitude. Six identical RUN cycles consume all 36 bits and leave the quotient in the low 32 bits. Unsigned trials and multiples need 34 bits of magnitude and an explicit borrow bit on subtraction. Apply the existing quotient/remainder selection and sign correction at completion. Us\n…[3568 of 6640 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e0d53bf89998b67c]…\n  47.7,\n    47.7\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      45.417,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      47.7,\n      21\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      47.7,\n      21\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 8,\n  \"bsram\": 6,\n  \"dsp\": 6,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -17.018,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 27.313,\n    \"logic_cells\": 15,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 15,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T03:11:14.666978Z\",\n  \"slot\": 1,\n  \"round_id\": 2,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r2s1 (improvement, +49.09%): Registering 3\\u00d7 the divisor and testing all three multiples in parallel cut divider feedback from eight serial restoring steps per clock to three radix-4 decisions, raising Fmax at no cycle cost in CoreMark\\u2019s divide-free timed loop.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
