{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git status --short && ls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r3s1.yaml && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r3s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 4073 Nov 22 04:43 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r3s1.yaml\nid: hyp-20261122-002-r3s1\ntitle: Resolve older operand dependencies before execute\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten timed iterations at 47.7 MHz. In the median Gowin placement, a register-file BSRAM output feeds EX branch resolution and returns through hazard control to an ID/EX operand register in 26.259 ns. The other read port feeds a dmem address input through forwarding and the multiplier in 26.246 ns. Both paths pay the cost of selecting EX operands before the actual computation begins.\nhypothesis: |\n  At decode, assemble each source from the register file, the current WB write, or the result completing in MEM. Give MEM first priority and WB second. Capture that value at the existing ID/EX boundary. Only the immediately preceding producer can still supersede it. While the consumer is in ID, compare its two source addresses with the nonzero destination in ID/EX and register the two match bits beside the operands. In EX each source needs one 2:1 mux controlled by its match bit and the EX/MEM producer's trap-resolved write enable.\n\n  Use two distributed asynchronous-read RAM replicas so each ID/EX operand flop captures a completed read. Drive speculative read addresses and match comparisons from raw imem instruction fields. Let valid and control bits squash bubbles. Hold both captured values and producer matches on backpressure. For loads, tap the existing aligned, extended MEM result and admit it only when the pipeline advances. The one-cycle load-use interlock still applies. A trapping producer must leave the previous architectural value available.\n\n  An isolated RTL prototype reached 59.985, 61.085 and 61.085 MHz across the three Gowin placement options. Stalled CoreMark completed in 4,491,485 marker-bracketed cycles with all five expected CRCs. That gives 136.00 iterations/s, 28.1% above the 106.20 champion. The median placement's limiting path now\n…[1115 of 4187 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8ebcee37eabc7f29]…\nX with the advanced producer's reg_write. A held instruction retains its match bits.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire raw fetch source addresses to the RF and match logic. Select a qualified MEM value per matching source ahead of the write-first RF outputs at the ID inputs. Keep PC, instruction metadata and load-use hazard control on their existing issue schedule.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Feed each EX operand from its captured ID value or the adjacent EX/MEM result. Use these operands for the ALU, divider launch, branches, JALR, store data and RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: Check both replicas after a warm reset and after same-address read/write collisions, including x0.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise consecutive writers to one rd followed by a two-source consumer, a dependent byte load held by dmem backpressure, and a trapping misaligned load followed by a consumer of its old rd. Check RVFI operands, result and retirement order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
