{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261122-003-r5s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move DIV and REM off the single-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 iterations/s at 5.442 MHz. Gowin reports a 199.837 ns path through operand forwarding and the EX ALU with 156 cells. The ALU computes signed and unsigned quotient and remainder combinationally. Full-width division is the strongest candidate for that depth.\\n\\nDisassembly of the canonical RV32IM -O3 CoreMark binary shows exactly five DIVU instructions, all in main. The measured start_time, iterate and stop_time calls are at 0x1220, 0x1228 and 0x122c. Neither iterate nor any of its callees contains a DIV or REM instruction. Moving division across clock edges therefore carries no direct latency cost in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 iterations/s at 5.442 MHz. Gowin reports a 199.837 ns path through operand forwarding and the EX ALU with 156 cells. The ALU computes signed and unsigned quotient and remainder combinationally. Full-width division is the strongest candidate for that depth.\\n\\nDisassembly of the canonical RV32IM -O3 CoreMark binary shows exactly five DIVU instructions, all in main. The measured start_time, iterate and stop_time calls are at 0x1220, 0x1228 and 0x122c. Neither iterate nor any of its callees contains a DIV or REM instruction. Moving division across clock edges therefore carries no direct latency cost in the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU one shared, blocking restoring divider in EX. Capture the forwarded operands and sign flags at issue. Run four registered rounds of eight binary quotient steps each on unsigned magnitudes. Each step uses the borrow from a trial 