3.248 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Feed the registered port address from bypassed rs1 plus the signed\n      I/S offset. Select instruction bits 11:7 for a store or 24:20 for a\n      load as the low five offset bits, with bits 31:25 shared.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the port address and next EX reservation when EX/MEM\n      advances. Pending EX memory work selects its forwarded-base address\n      and clears the reservation. Otherwise choose the ID address and\n      capture rs1_ready. Hold both across a MEM wait. Select request\n      enables and store data by the registered owner. Send only pending MEM\n      operations to the stall logic and only unfinished EX loads to the\n      load-use check. Forward the registered early-load or ALU value.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend EX/MEM with early acceptance, an early-load selector, raw bus\n      response and extended load result. Keep the effective address and\n      forwarded store operand with their instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Supply forwarded rs1 plus the I/S displacement for the retry address.\n      Form a request from the registered port address, validated controls,\n      width and forwarded store data. Gate off misalignment. On acceptance\n      capture the response, extended value and selectors together with\n      the EX/MEM packet. Keep the ALU result and early load in parallel\n      registers so the load selection follows the register edge.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Suppress the request for an early completion. For that instruction\n      use the saved word for RVFI and the saved extended value for decode\n      bypass and writeback. Serve pending instructions with the usual lane\n      extraction, trap and memory backpressure. Use the same architectural\n      address, masks and data whichever stage performed the transfer.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Verify adjacent retirement after an accepted EX byte, halfword or\n      word load. Deny an early store for several clocks and check address,\n      data and byte enables on each attempt, followed by one handshake.\n      Exercise a busy base, a dependent store value, two contenders for\n      the port, misalignment, MMIO, and a wrong-path store. Check RVFI\n      order and operands. Adapt timing-specific assertions to distinguish\n      an accepted EX access from a request retried in MEM.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=next(Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses').glob('*r6s1.yaml'))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'p=\"$TMPDIR/r6s1-bench-2am7678a\"\ncat > \"$p/formal_variant.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport pathlib, sys, shutil, os, subprocess\np=pathlib.Path(__file__).parent/sys.argv[1]\nroot=pathlib.Path.cwd()\nf=p/'formal'\nr=f/'riscv-formal'\nr.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor n in ['run_all.sh','wrapper_si.sv','checks_si.cfg']:\n shutil.copy(root/'formal'/n,f/n)\nfor n in ['insns','checks']:\n if not (r/n).exists(): (r/n).symlink_to((root/'formal/riscv-formal'/n).resolve())\nenv=dict(os.environ,RTL_DIR='rtl',CORE_NAME='bench',WRAPPER=str(f/'wrapper_si.sv'),CHECKS_CFG=str(f/'checks_si.cfg'),JOBS='5')\nwith (p/'formal.log').open('w') as out:\n rc=subprocess.run(['bash',str(f/'run_all.sh')],env=env,cwd=p,stdout=out,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)\nprint((p/'formal.log').read_text()[-1000:])\nsys.exit(rc.returncode)\nPY\npython3 \\\"\"'$p/formal_variant.py\" dispatch'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
