{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'DIV|REM|divid|multipl|MUL' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py && cat bench/programs/Makefile && rg -n -i 'max.cycles|markers|coremark|uart|trac' test/cosim/main.cpp | tail -58 && ls -l /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh && python -c 'import jsonschema,yaml'\"", "aggregated_output": "70:def DIV (rd, rs1, rs2):  return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 4, rd, 0x33)\n71:def DIVU(rd, rs1, rs2):  return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 5, rd, 0x33)\n72:def REM (rd, rs1, rs2):  return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 6, rd, 0x33)\n73:def REMU(rd, rs1, rs2):  return _r(1, rs2, rs1, 7, rd, 0x33)\n582:async def dependent_divides_with_stalled_memory(dut):\n586:        DIV(3, 1, 2),       # use the load's forwarded -103\n587:        REM(4, 1, 3),       # use the quotient as a negative divisor\n590:        DIVU(6, 5, 5),      # held in EX behind the stalled store\n591:        REMU(7, 2, 6),\n614:    # before the divider finishes, must reach RVFI with the result.\n628:    # Load-use adds a bubble. The stalled store must advance before DIVU\nCROSS   := riscv32-unknown-elf\nCC      := $(CROSS)-gcc\n\n# CoreMark build knobs. Defaults are the canonical EEMBC reporting config\n# (2K data size, -O3); tools/eval/fpga.py's COREMARK_EXPECTED CRCs assume\n# exactly these defaults.\n# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\n#   the EEMBC canonical reporting config (used by VexRiscv et al.); 6000\n#   makes the matrix/list/state working sets ~3x larger so the score is\n#   harder to inflate via register-resident working sets.\n# - COREMARK_OPT: gcc optimization. -O3 is the standard CoreMark publication\n#   flag; -O2 is what the V0 baseline used.\n# Defaults match VexRiscv's published CoreMark methodology so the\n# orchestrator's fitness number is directly comparable to public CoreMark\n# results. To override (e.g. for the prior 6K -O2 V0 baseline):\n#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nCOREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000\nCOREMARK_OPT  ?= -O3\n\nCFLAGS  := -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 $(COREMARK_OPT) -static -nostartfiles \\\n           -specs=nano.specs -specs=nosys.specs \\\n           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\n           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\n           -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=$(COREMARK_SIZE)\n\nSRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\n        bench\n…[1758 of 4830 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:848f8097c8330b25]…\nurn 0.\n130:        //   - dmem write: UART range is allowed (TX); BENCH_START/STOP are\n131:        //     allowed (markers); anything else outside dmem is OOB (handled\n150:            // MMIO UART at 0x10000000: capture to uart_buf, don't route to dmem\n152:            // BENCH_START/BENCH_STOP markers at 0x10000100 / 0x10000104: record\n154:            // and exclude CoreMark init/CRC-printing from the timing window.\n159:                // Last stop_time() call wins — CoreMark calls it once, but\n162:            } else if (in_uart_range(addr)) {\n166:                        if (c) uart_buf.push_back(c);\n172:                // OOB write (neither dmem nor UART). Flag so testbench reports it.\n179:        // Drain channel 0 then channel 1 (NRET=2 contract). For V0\n257:        // Escape backslash/quote/newline in uart_buf for JSON string safety.\n259:        for (char c : uart_buf) {\n269:               \"\\\"bench_bracketed\\\":%s,\\\"uart\\\":\\\"%s\\\"}\\n\",\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 nobody nogroup 24968 Jul 10  2025 /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
