{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_98", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r7s1.yaml')\nimport textwrap\ns=p.read_text().replace('4,039 logic cells, nine block RAMs and two DSPs.', '4,039 logic cells, nine block RAMs and two DSPs. The scratch build passed all five cocotb suites and the selftest and three random reference traces on both ready and stalled buses.')\nout=[]\nfor line in s.splitlines():\n if len(line)>100 and line.lstrip()[0] not in {'-'} and line.startswith(' '):\n  indent=line[:len(line)-len(line.lstrip())]\n  out.extend(textwrap.wrap(line.strip(), width=84, initial_indent=indent, subsequent_indent=indent,break_long_words=False,break_on_hyphens=False))\n else:\n  out.append(line)\np.write_text('\\\\n'.join(out)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nsed -n '1,55p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r7s1.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261122-002-r7s1\ntitle: Bank execute results at EX/MEM and write the register file on MEM completion\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  At the champion's median placement, three paths are within 0.03 ns of one another.\n  They run from the replay RAM through register reads to the fetch PC, from\n  forwarding through a multiplier to EX/MEM, and through the divider's quotient\n  recurrence. Moving every multiply into a blocking unit added 187,665 marked cycles\n  in a scratch run. The execution pipeline needs to produce a multiply on every\n  advancing edge.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make MEM the point where execution results meet. Capture the full product beside\n  the ordinary EX/MEM result. Select its high half, its low half or the ordinary\n  result from registered controls. Forward the selected value to the adjacent\n  instruction and write the register file when MEM completes. Decode sees that write\n  through the file's write-first port. Fetch takes the array output before the\n  bypass and uses its existing operand-based predictions only when all required\n  values are already in the array.\n\n  Fit division to the same result boundary by splitting the radix-4 recurrence at\n  divisor magnitude 256. A smaller divisor needs at most an eight-bit partial\n  remainder. A larger divisor already exceeds the top byte of any 32-bit dividend,\n  leaving only 24 quotient bits to calculate. Both paths fit the existing six RUN\n  edges. This removes the three-deep chain of full-width trial selections without\n  adding a stall to any RV32M operation.\n\n  A scratch implementation completed ten iterations in 3,132,302 marked cycles with\n  both bus stalls and all five expected CRCs, versus 3,122,498 for the champion.\n  Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 68.729, 72.115 and 72.115 MHz with one\n  registered enable per result bank. The median gives 230.23 iterations/s, 11.98%\n  above 205.60. The acceptance threshold at this cycle count is 67.363 MHz. Gowin\n  used 4,039 logic cells, nine block RAMs and two DSPs. The scratch build passed all\n  five cocotb suites and the selftest and three random reference traces on both\n  ready and stalled buses.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Give one signed 33-by-33 multiplier the two forwarded register operands\n      directly. Sign-extend both for MULH, only rs1 for MULHSU, and neither for MUL\n      or MULHU. Register the low 64 product bits on EX/MEM advance and expose both\n      halves. Register the exact per-op ALTOPS result on the same edge. For DIV/REM,\n      capture unsigned magnitudes and sign flags on start. In PREP register 3D for\n      each radix-4 path. For 1 <= D < 256, begin with R=0 and a 36-bit zero-padded\n      dividend. Emit three radix-4 digits per RUN edge using 10-bit trials and an\n      explicit borrow. For D >= 256, initialize R from the dividend's top byte and\n      consume its remaining 24 bits MSB first, two radix-4 digits per edge with\n      34-bit trials and an explicit borrow. Select the proper magnitude in DONE,\n      apply sign correction, and return all ones or the original dividend on divide\n      or remainder by zero. Keep the same start, PREP, six RUN edges, held DONE, and\n      consume timing in real and ALTOPS builds.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
