{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_151", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > 'cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r8s1.yaml' <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-002-r8s1\ntitle: Move the load-use interlock behind EX/MEM and forward completed misses from WB\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  In the champion's 71.73 MHz Gowin placement the worst path starts at\n  rs1_match_q, crosses the EX base mux, address adder and load-tag comparison,\n  and ends at the fetch predecessor register's clock enable. A younger\n  instruction already knows whether it names the load's destination in ID.\n  Only the load's hit or miss remains to be resolved. Registering those two\n  facts independently takes address verification out of the fetch issue path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Admit the successor of a load into ID/EX. On that edge, capture one bit\n  indicating a match with the preceding load's nonzero rd. In parallel, the\n  load captures its verified hit in EX/MEM. A hit uses the existing adjacent\n  forwarding path. An independent instruction executes normally. For a\n  dependent miss, hold the consumer, its two source matches and the fetch PC.\n  When the load completes, let it retire into MEM/WB and insert a bubble in\n  EX/MEM. On the next cycle, a fourth input to the existing result bus supplies\n  MEM/WB.rd_data to each matched operand. The other operand comes from its\n  ID/EX latch. This keeps a single bubble on dependent misses and consecutive\n  retirements on hits, including when the consumer is a branch or multiply.\n  \n  A scratch prototype completed ten iterations with both stall generators in\n  3,132,302 marked cycles, matching the champion, with all five canonical CRCs\n  and the validation banner. Gowin placement option 1 reached 76.442 MHz.\n  The replacement threshold at this cycle count is 75.03 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture the OR of the two source matches against a nonzero EX load\n      destination when ID advances. Qualify it with consumer valid and the\n      registered EX/MEM miss to request repair. Hold the bit during a MEM wait\n      and clear it when MEM drains while ID stays held. Feed the registered\n      MEM/WB result into EX's forwarding network. Keep the individual source\n      matches frozen through repair and qualify them with the normal writer\n      enable or the registered repair-forward enable. Advance load-address\n      history only on a real EX execution.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the combinational EX-load-hit-to-ID flush with a hold for the\n      registered dependent miss. A pending bus request holds EX/MEM as usual.\n      On the completion edge, allow MEM/WB and EX/MEM to advance while holding\n      IF and ID/EX for one cycle. Branch recovery keeps its normal flush.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      During repair suppress redirect, predictor training and divide launch.\n      On completion clear EX/MEM valid and side-effect controls and deselect\n      the ordinary and product banks. Set the fourth bank's forwarding enable\n      only if the completing load actually writes a register. A faulting load\n      consequently leaves the consumer's captured values available. A stalled\n      load cannot expose unaccepted dmem data. The bubble never retires.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check an adjacent hit and miss with both sources matching under dmem\n      backpressure. Assert the same exact retirement gaps and memory handshakes.\n      Check the fetch PC advances past the admitted consumer and holds there\n      through repair. Verify recovered operands, branch targets, store data,\n      fault suppression, divide start and consecutive channel-0 orders.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r8s1.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(f.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('validated',f)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
