-bit destination row. Keep two issued PCs' prediction metadata. When a live bus word at Q issues, train the older PC's exception if Q's row differs from its sequential prediction, or clear its previously matched exception if the stream returned to sequential execution. Buffer the fill and training transaction for one cycle.\\n\\nFill a 1,024-word block RAM at Q[11:2] with the instruction, a valid bit and the full in-window word PC. Read the\n…[3700 of 6772 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7cf122eb33eea090]…\n on the multicycle-divider champion'), ('hyp-20261122-003-r3s2', 'predictor', 'Predict control transfers from ready operands during fetch'), ('hyp-20261122-003-r4s2', 'predictor', 'Predict equality branches from decode operands and register the recovery PC'), ('hyp-20261122-003-r5s2', 'predictor', 'Predict the next instruction word from the issuing PC'), ('hyp-20261122-003-r6s2', 'predictor', \"Predict a load's data RAM row one cycle before its address resolves\"), ('hyp-20261122-003-r7s2', 'predictor', 'Read instruction operands one cycle early from the predicted next PC'), ('hyp-20261122-002-r8s1', 'structural', \"Select the adjacent producer's result bank separately for each EX operand\"), ('hyp-20261122-003-r8s2', 'predictor', 'Issue a dependent instruction on a predicted load hit and repair a miss in place'), ('hyp-20261122-002-r9s1', 'structural', 'Give fetch a dedicated operand path from the live instruction bus'), ('hyp-20261122-003-r9s2', 'predictor', 'Predict the instruction RAM row two issues ahead')]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
