{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_126","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r10s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"Probe the two-issue fetch predictor on every clock\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,131,081 bracketed cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Its reported option-0 Gowin path runs from the EX operand-forwarding select rs1_high_q to the instruction replay block RAM. The RAM already knows the predicted row from the fetch PC. Its read enable still waits for the load-use and branch-recovery decisions that qualify issue.\nhypothesis: |\n  Read the predicted instruction row on every clock. Qualify the response one cycle later with a registered copy of issue. On the cycle after an accepted probe, save the RAM response and its collision/scrub qualification in a fabric holding register. At the next issue, advance the live response if the preceding clock issued, or the saved response if a stall or redirect intervened. This gives the existing two-issue predictor the same sequence of candidates with a constant block-RAM read enable.\n\n  Keep the response data and its validity together across arbitrary gaps. Reset and issued FENCE.I invalidate both the in-flight and saved response. Continue to train and fill from accepted instructions, give a ready bus word priority, and require the full in-window PC match before replay. Removing the late EX-to-RAM control path should raise median Fmax at the same cycle count. The acceptance threshold at that count is 89.45 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Make the predicted-row RAM read unconditional. Register probe acceptance and read/write collision status, capture the last accepted response, and align the replay candidate with the next issue across holds, redirects and fence invalidation.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise uninterrupted replay and one- and multi-clock gaps between probe and use. Include a redirect during a gap, a colliding fill on the accepted probe, and FENCE.I while a saved response is pending. Check issued PCs and retired instructions with the instruction bus stalled.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
