{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_107", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r11s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-003-r11s2\ntitle: Predict dependent load rows from the producer and refetch a consumer on a false hit\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  In round 10, 94,913 of 108,865 load-table misses had an adjacent writer\n  of the base register. A stride indexed by the load PC has little\n  information about a pointer just read from a linked list. The producer\n  has a candidate pointer or operands for an address sum a cycle earlier.\n  The champion also puts full load-address verification on the path\n  that enables the instruction replay RAM.\nhypothesis: |\n  On issue of a load with a pending base and a displacement from -4 to +3\n  bytes, probe the producer's predicted word row. For an LW producer,\n  take bits 11:2 of its raw RAM response. Otherwise preview the low\n  12-bit sum of the producer's registered ID/EX operands, selecting its\n  immediate for an immediate operation. Use the inputs before forwarding.\n  Stale operands, other opcodes and a displacement crossing a word can\n  all give a wrong row. For other pending bases use the existing stride\n  row. For ready bases use the normal base-plus-displacement probe.\n\n  Allow the next instruction to enter ID/EX assuming the load will hit.\n  Register the candidate's coherence permission, tag and provisional value\n  alongside the resolved byte address. MEM checks the entire aligned\n  word address, the RAM window, validity and access alignment before\n  suppressing a bus read. If verification fails and the instruction in\n  EX actually carries an adjacent forwarding match to this load, discard\n  that execution and refetch its own PC on MEM completion. This lets ID\n  reread the committed register value, including the old register value\n  after a trapping load. A consumer of a verified hit can retire one\n  cycle after its producer. An independent instruction needs no retry.\n\n  A scratch implementation took 3,063,566 marked cycles for ten iterations\n  versus 3,131,081 for the champion, with all five CRCs and the validation\n  banner. At that cycle count the 4.6% replacement margin requires more\n  than 87.52 MHz. Placement 1 reached 85.769 MHz. Timing is the remaining\n  risk for this prediction scheme.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Select the producer hint, ready-base sum or stride probe. Remove the unverified full-address verdict from the decode interlock. Retain the dmem and divide holds.\n  - file: rtl/load_predictor.sv\n    description: Add the producer row input to the synchronous probe. Keep delayed stride training, reset scrub, full word tags, read/write collision rejection and the older-store veto aligned with the candidate.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Carry provisional hit metadata into EX/MEM. Use the verified verdict for the MEM request and RVFI. Give a valid dependent retry priority over branch recovery, suppress its EX/MEM valid and controls, branch training and divide launch, and redirect exactly once when the older memory operation completes.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise a warmed irregular pointer chain, an incorrect producer hint, an aliased page and a misaligned load feeding a store or branch. Check bus transfers, exact RVFI values and single retirement during delayed completion. Check the extra fetch of the dependent PC on a false hit and adjacent retirement on a verified hit.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r11s2.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(273.11*1.046*3063566/10e6)\nPY\nfor name in probe21 probe22 probe23 probe24; do tail -1 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/$name/timing/gowin_p1/gw.log\"; done'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
