{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"agent_message","text":"The first prototype completed CoreMark with all five expected CRCs, but its indirect-target check lengthened the recovery path. The cycle profile also shows that eliminating every branch redirect would save only about 1.5% on this core. I’ll test a simpler way to predict the replay RAM address while keeping the existing single-cycle branch recovery."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_73", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat > \"$TMPDIR/xor.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom shutil import copytree\nimport os,sys\nt=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR']); dest,*flags=sys.argv[1:];p=t/dest/'rtl'; copytree('cores/bench/rtl',p);d=p/'if_stage.sv';s=d.read_text()\ndef r(a,b):\n global s\n assert a in s,a\n s=s.replace(a,b)\nr('logic [14:0] exceptions','logic [9:0] exceptions')\nsz=11 if '2k' in flags else 10\niw=8 if '256' in flags else 9 if '512' in flags else 7\n# Rotate destination-indexed block RAM and predict its physical address with one asynchronous RAM.\nr('  assign sequential_row = pc[11:2] + 10\\\\'d2;\\\\n  assign exception_entry = exceptions[pc[8:2]];\\\\n  assign matched = exception_entry.valid && exception_entry.tag == pc[12:9];\\\\n  assign read_row = matched ? exception_entry.row : sequential_row;', '''  logic [9:0] rotation, correction;\n  assign rotation = pc[11:2] - 10'd2;\n  assign correction = exceptions[pc[8:2]];\n  assign matched = |correction;\n  assign read_row = pc[11:2] \"'^ correction;'\"''')\nr('  assign write_row = scrub[10] ? fill_pc_q[11:2]', '''  logic [9:0] fill_row_q, update_delta_q;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    fill_row_q <= rotation;\n    update_delta_q <= rotation \"'^ older.source[11:2];\n  end\n  assign write_row = scrub[10] ? fill_row_q'\"''')\nr('exceptions[exception_write_index] <= {scrub[10] && exception_valid_q,\\\\n                                             source_q[12:9], fill_pc_q[11:2]};','exceptions[exception_write_index] <= scrub[10] ? update_delta_q : 10\\\\'b0;')\nr('history_valid[1] && (nonsequential || older.matched)','history_valid[1]' if 'all' in flags else 'history_valid[1] && (nonsequential || older.matched)')\nr('        read_ok_q <= scrub[10] && \"'!(fill_q && read_row == fill_pc_q[11:2]);'\"\\\\n        candidate_ok_q <= read_ok_q;', '''        read_ok_q <= scrub[10];\n        candidate_ok_q <= read_ok_q && \"