{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' or d.get('id','').endswith('r3s1'):\n  print(d['id'],list(d))\n  for k in ['hypothesis','implementation_notes','metrics','fitness']:print(k,d.get(k))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 ['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'IF and ID share a cycle in this core. Fetch always selects PC+4, so a taken\\ntransfer resolved in EX discards one fetch slot. Between the MMIO markers,\\n294,425 conditional branches select a nonsequential PC and 49,367 JALs\\nexecute. With both bus stalls enabled, the 128-entry prototype completed\\nten CoreMark iterations in 4,202,272 bracketed cycles and matched all five\\ncanonical CRCs. This saves 289,213 cycles and raises iterations/cycle by 6.88%.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Use the fetched instruction to identify legal conditional branches and JAL.\\nIn parallel with immediate generation, read a 128-entry table of two-bit\\nsaturating counters indexed by the fetch PC. For a conditional branch use\\nthe counter MSB, and for JAL predict taken. Select the aligned PC-relative\\ntarget on a taken prediction and PC+4 otherwise. JALR resolves in EX.\\nComputing direct targets from the current instruction makes table aliasing\\naffect only direction and requires just one prediction bit per instruction.\\n\\nAfter initialization, train once per valid conditional branch advancing\\nfrom EX. A correct prediction lets an accepted fetch enter ID/EX on the\\nresolution edge.\\nA mismatch flushes that fetch and loads the architectural successor into\\nthe PC. The prototype's three Gowin placement options reached 5.155,\\n5.488 and 5.488 MHz. Combining the median with the measured cycle count\\nyields 13.06 iter/s, 7.75% above the 12.12 baseline. Placement option 0\\nused 533 additional logic cells and 265 additional registers.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 8, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [\n…[15365 of 18437 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2aec092ff17d29ce]…\nl branch by saturating\\nits captured counter toward the actual direction and writing at the\\nresolving PC index. A concurrent same-index fetch can use the old\\ncounter. A dmem freeze defers both training and recovery until release.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Qualify load-use comparisons against the raw fetch fields with imem_ready so an undelivered instruction cannot request a dependency stall.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check fetch addresses on ready signed and unsigned branches, busy\\nloop predictions and loop exit. Cover a JALR using WB bypass, one\\nusing EX/MEM, and one with two pending writers to rs1 where the\\nyounger writer must win. Exercise an unavailable load result,\\nnonzero JALR offset, bit-zero clearing and a misaligned target.\\nHold a branch behind a stalled data access and deny imem on the\\nrecovery edge. Check RVFI successor, link, trap and order, plus\\nsuppression of a wrong-path store.\\n'}]}\nimplementation_notes \nmetrics None\nfitness 122.65\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
