{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'predictor|predict' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in sys.stdin];print(list(rows[-1])); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(str(row)[:1900] for row in rows))'\"", "aggregated_output": "['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n{'id': 'hyp-20261122-001-r1s0', 'title': 'Resolve two quotient bits per step in the combinational divider', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'motivation': \"The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path runs from the MEM/WB destination\\nregister through forwarding and the EX ALU. The ALU evaluates signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. A chain of quotient-bit\\ndecisions is a plausible source of the reported 156-cell path. Shortening\\nit would raise the clock rate for every CoreMark instruction.\\n\", 'hypothesis': {'motivation': \"The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path runs from the MEM/WB destination\\nregister through forwarding and the EX ALU. The ALU evaluates signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. A chain of quotient-bit\\ndecisions is a plausible source of the reported 156-cell path. Shortening\\nit would raise the clock rate for every CoreMark instruction.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unrolled radix-4 restoring\\ndivider inside the ALU. Each of 16 steps consumes two dividend bits and\\ncomputes three trial differences in parallel. Their borrow flags select\\nboth the next quotient digit and an already computed remainder. This\\nhalves the number of serial digit deci