{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json, pprint\nD=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nfor d in D[-3:]:\n for k in ['id','hypothesis','changes','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path','seeds','perturbations']:\n  print(k,d[k])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id hyp-20261122-001-r5s0\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The champion waits for EX/MEM before presenting every data request. When\\ndecode already has the correct base and the older instruction leaves the\\ndata port idle, that costs a bus opportunity. An adjacent load consumer\\nalso takes a bubble even when RAM could have returned the word in EX.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Compute the effective address in decode from its bypassed rs1 and the\\nsigned I/S displacement. A valid, aligned RAM load or store with a ready\\nbase can use the idle data port in EX. On acceptance, capture the result\\nand mark the access complete. A dependent consumer can immediately use\\nthe registered load result through the existing EX/MEM forwarding path.\\nAn outstanding older access takes priority. A denied early request\\ncontinues in MEM at the same address with the same lanes and store data.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations with both bus stalls and the\\nfive canonical CRCs in 3,920,825 marked cycles, down from 4,164,193.\\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 65.170, 65.099 and 65.099 MHz.\\nThe median gives 166.03 iterations/s, 6.79% above the 155.48 champion.\\nAt this cycle count the acceptance threshold requires more than 63.765 MHz.\\nPlacement option 0 used 3,635 logic cells and 749 registers. The prototype\\npassed all 53 fast formal checks, all five cocotb suites with updated\\npipeline coverage, and the selftest and three random reference traces\\nwith and without bus stalls.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 7, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add the signed 12-bit offset to the MEM/WB-bypassed rs1. Bits 11:5\\nof the offset come from instruction bits 31:25. Opcode bit 5 selects\\ninstruction bits 11:7 for stores or 24:20 for loads. Capture the sum\\ninto ID/EX and register the existing rs1 readiness in parallel on the\\nsame operand-capture edge. Expose the decode sum to the bus address\\nregister as well.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry the early ad\n…[16984 of 20056 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dd86b4b88e0e70b7]…\nh\\nregister-file addresses, source readiness and forwarding matches.\\nFeed effective fetch validity to the existing load-use and PC\\ninterlocks. Qualify the predictor's issue pulse with if_id_w.valid,\\n!stall_id and !flush_id. Keep EX redirect priority over a fetch hold.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a loop, then drive unrelated data on a stalled instruction bus\\nduring trained fetches. Check RVFI instruction words, PC sequence,\\norder and store results across a data stall and loop exit. Exercise\\ncolliding predecessor indices with different successor addresses\\nand verify fresh code after a stalled store followed by FENCE.I.\\n'}]\nfitness 184.82\nfmax_mhz 62.73\ncycles 3394055\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_21_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.63, 'arrival_ns': 21.925, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nseeds [60.131, 62.73, 62.73]\nperturbations [[0, 60.131, 11], [1, 62.73, 21], [2, 62.73, 21]]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
