{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'predictor|successor' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l)\n print(list(d)) if \\\"once\\\" not in globals() else None\n once=1\n print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"coremark_cycles\\\")})\n if \\\"predict\\\" in str(d.get(\\\"category\\\")) or \\\"r6s2\\\" in str(d.get(\\\"id\\\")): print(str(d)[:6500])'\"", "aggregated_output": "['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n{'id': 'hyp-20261122-003-r1s2', 'title': 'Predict direct branches at fetch with a 128-entry bimodal table', 'category': 'predictor', 'fitness': 12.91, 'cycles': 4202272}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261122-003-r1s2', 'title': 'Predict direct branches at fetch with a 128-entry bimodal table', 'category': 'predictor', 'motivation': 'IF and ID share a cycle in this core. Fetch always selects PC+4, so a taken\\ntransfer resolved in EX discards one fetch slot. Between the MMIO markers,\\n294,425 conditional branches select a nonsequential PC and 49,367 JALs\\nexecute. With both bus stalls enabled, the 128-entry prototype completed\\nten CoreMark iterations in 4,202,272 bracketed cycles and matched all five\\ncanonical CRCs. This saves 289,213 cycles and raises iterations/cycle by 6.88%.\\n', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'IF and ID share a cycle in this core. Fetch always selects PC+4, so a taken\\ntransfer resolved in EX discards one fetch slot. Between the MMIO markers,\\n294,425 conditional branches select a nonsequential PC and 49,367 JALs\\nexecute. With both bus stalls enabled, the 128-entry prototype completed\\nten CoreMark iterations in 4,202,272 bracketed cycles and matched all five\\ncanonical CRCs. This saves 289,213 cycles and raises iterations/cycle by 6.88%.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Use the fetched instruction to identify legal conditional branches and JAL.\\nIn parallel with immediate generation, read a 128-entry table of two-bit\\nsaturating counters indexed by the fetch PC. For a conditional branch use\\nthe counter MSB, and for JAL predict taken. Select the aligned PC-relative\\ntarget on a taken prediction and PC+4 otherwise. JALR resolves in EX.\n…[38034 of 41106 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:92f871c69ed78d74]…\ndress from the decode sum\\nor a 128-entry PC[8:2] stride table. Each stride entry records the\\nlast actual byte address modulo 4096 and the predicted next word\\nindex. Initialize the two distributed RAM arrays to zero at FPGA\\nconfiguration. At each advancing load, compute the next byte address\\nas (2 * actual - previous) modulo 4096 and store bits [11:2].\\nCapture the prior address at issue so each array needs one read\\nport and one write port. Hold the candidate with its EX instruction\\nthrough stalls. Each word-table row contains a\\nvalid bit, the full in-RAM word address and a 32-bit raw word.\\nRefill on accepted in-window reads or aligned full-word RAM stores.\\nInvalidate the indexed row on any other accepted store. Mark a\\nsame-row read/write collision ineligible and veto the candidate\\nwhile an older same-row store occupies MEM. Reset cancels the\\ncandidate and scrubs the word table through its write port. Resume\\nhits and fills once all 1024 rows have been invalidated.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'd\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat test/cosim/build.sh && rg -n 'coremark|gcc|verilator|BENCH|ELF|riscv' Makefile && command -v verilator && command -v riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc && command -v gw_sh\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat test/cosim/build.sh && rg -n 'coremark|gcc|verilator|BENCH|ELF|riscv' Makefile && command -v verilator && command -v riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc && command -v gw_sh\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Build the Verilator-based cosim binary that drives `core` against an ELF\n# program. Produces $OBJ_DIR/cosim_sim (default: test/cosim/obj_dir/cosim_sim).\n#\n# RTL_DIR (default: rtl/) is globbed dynamically (with core_pkg.sv forced\n# first because its compilation-unit-scope typedefs and localparams must be\n# visible before any module references them). Hypotheses are allowed to add,\n# rename, or delete files inside rtl/, so a hardcoded file list would\n# silently break restructuring hypotheses.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\nCOSIM_DIR=\"$REPO_ROOT/test/cosim\"\nif [ -z \"${RTL_DIR:-}\" ] || [ -z \"${OBJ_DIR:-}\" ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: test/cosim/build.sh requires RTL_DIR and OBJ_DIR env vars.\" >&2\n  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl OBJ_DIR=cores/v1/obj_dir bash test/cosim/build.sh\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\n# NRET picks which RVFI port set main.cpp expects on `core`.\n# 1 = single-issue (only `_0` ports); 2 = dual-channel (both `_0` and `_1`).\n# Default 2 preserves existing behavior; orchestrator sets to 1 for cores\n# whose core.yaml declares nret: 1.\nNRET=\"${NRET:-2}\"\n\n# Ensure OSS CAD Suite tools are on PATH for non-interactive shells.\nTOOLCHAIN=\"$REPO_ROOT/.toolchain\"\nif [ -d \"$TOOLCHAIN/oss-cad-suite/bin\" ]; then\n  export PATH=\"$TOOLCHAIN/oss-cad-suite/bin:$PATH\"\nfi\n\nmkdir -p \"$OBJ_DIR\"\n\n# Glob $RTL_DIR/*.sv. core_pkg.sv first; the rest in a stable lexicographic\n# order (modulo case-insensitive sort, which Verilator/gcc don't care\n# about). If core_pkg.sv is missing the build will catch that downstream\n# via undefined-typedef errors.\nRTL_FILES=()\n[ -f \"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && RTL_FILES+=(\"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\")\nfor f in \"$RTL_DIR\"/*.sv; do\n  [ \"$(basename \"$f\")\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\n  RTL_FILES+=(\"$f\")\ndone\n\nif [ ${#RTL_FILES[@]} -eq 0 ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: no rtl/*.sv files found.\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nverilator --cc --exe --build \\\n  -Mdir \"$OBJ_DIR\" \\\n  \"+incdir+$RTL_DIR\" \\\n  --top-module core \\\n  -Wall -Wno-fatal -Wno-style \\\n  -CFLAGS \"-DNRET=$NRET\" \\\n  \"${RTL_FILES[@]}\" \\\n  \"$COSIM_DIR/main.cpp\" \\\n  -o cosim_sim\n\necho \"Built: $OBJ_DIR/cosim_sim\"\n42:  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\n77:\t@echo \"  make lint TARGET=v1     — verilator lint over cores/<TARGET>/rtl/*.sv\"\n80:\t@echo \"  make formal TARGET=v1   — riscv-formal fast suite (with ALTOPS)\"\n84:\t@echo \"  make bench              — build selftest + coremark ELFs\"\n94:# verilator lint over $(RTL_DIR)/.\n99:\t  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+$(RTL_DIR) \\\n112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\n137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\n143:bench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\n144:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.c) \\\n145:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.h) \\\n146:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.c) \\\n147:                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.h)\n148:\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/coremark.elf\n162:\t  [ -e \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\" ] || ln -s \"$(CURDIR)/formal/riscv-formal\" \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\"; \\\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/verilator\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
