{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()):\n if d['id'].endswith('r4s0'): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],d['hypothesis']['changes'])\nPY\ncommand -v riscv32-unknown-elf-objdump\"","aggregated_output":"Drive fetch from the resolved next PC of the instruction in EX. For an\naligned taken transfer this is the target. For a fall-through or a\ntrapping transfer it is the instruction's PC plus four. Pair the fetched\nword with that same address at ID. When both stages can advance, the\ntarget issues on the edge that moves the branch out of EX.\n\nReplace the existing fetch counter with a retry PC. Every cycle with a\nvalid instruction in EX saves its resolved successor, including during\na stall. An EX bubble selects the saved PC, so a missed target can be\nretried after the branch leaves EX. This keeps a second incrementer\noff the path from branch resolution to the next request.\n\nThe isolated prototype took 4,136,096 marker-bracketed cycles for ten\niterations with both bus stalls, down from 4,491,485. All five CoreMark\nCRCs matched. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 63.321, 62.307\nand 62.307 MHz. The median gives 150.64 iterations/s, 7.99% above\n139.50. All 53 single-retire fast formal checks passed.\n [{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export a combinational ex_next_pc using the existing aligned redirect\\ndecision to select redirect_target or in.pc + 4. Capture this same\\nvalue in EX/MEM.pc_next for RVFI. Preserve the forwarded comparison\\noperands, JALR bit-zero clearing and misalignment trap logic.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Reset retry_pc to zero and latch ex_next_pc on every id_ex.valid\\ncycle. Drive imem_addr and out.pc from id_ex.valid ? ex_next_pc :\\nretry_pc. Use the existing NOP and invalid payload on an imem stall.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Set flush_if on an imem stall. Set flush_id for a load-use hazard\\nwhen neither dmem nor divide holds ID/EX. Retire the stall_if output\\nand redirect input. Keep the existing ID/EX and EX/MEM holds so a\\nbranch waiting behind a stalled memory operation issues its target\\nexactly once when downstream accepts it.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire id_ex_w.valid and ex_next_pc to IF. Remove the former stall_if\\nand EX redirect connections to the hazard unit. Continue to sample\\nthe RF reads and forwarding matches for the selected fetch word on\\nthe existing operand-capture enable.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'On ready buses, check consecutive retirements through a JAL, a\\nlink consumer, an odd-address JALR and a taken conditional branch.\\nExercise a stalled older store with the target initially ready, then\\ndeassert imemReady as the store completes. Check the repeated target\\naddress, retirement PCs and order, link value and accepted stores.\\n'}]\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/bin/riscv32-unknown-elf-objdump\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
