X repair\\nvalues back to these same registers with priority on the repair edge.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'For a pending multiply, wait behind an older stalled memory request,\\nthen sample both resolved EX sources exactly once. Hold ID/EX and\\nfeed a bubble to EX/MEM on that edge as for a waiting divide. On\\nthe following advance use the product and the saved source values,\\ninclud\n…[7572 of 10644 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ad7435d5b729a72c]…\ncollision veto as the block RAM. Launch the read\\nusing EX recovery first, the predicted successor on issue, and the\\nheld PC otherwise. Carry the sampled row and suppress collisions.\\nOn a bus wait, admit a word only if its entire in-window address\\nmatches. Give ready bus data priority. Reset and issued FENCE.I\\ncancel pending replay and scrub all rows through the write port.\\nHold younger issue while the fence waits behind an older store.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry the predicted target word address, predicted-taken bit and\\na precomputed direct-target match through IF/ID and ID/EX.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture the prediction with its instruction and hold both on a freeze.\\nCompare the BTB target with the direct target computed from the fetched\\nword on the issue side of the ID/EX register.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Recover on a direction mismatch or a wrong destination on a taken\\nprediction. Compare JALR against its full forwa\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
