{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r8s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-003-r8s2\ntitle: Predict a load bypass at issue and repair dependent misses in EX\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion already predicts a data RAM row for each load, but issue waits\n  for EX to prove the hit. The forwarded base, effective-address addition,\n  tag comparison and load-use interlock can all feed the fetch predictor's\n  issue enable in one cycle. The reported worst path starts at the rs1\n  forwarding select and ends at the successor table's predecessor register.\n  The previous instruction-replay improvement saved only 17,102 cycles.\n  Shortening the issue decision offers a larger opportunity at 71.73 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict that an adjacent load will supply its result from the existing\n  word table. Admit its consumer to ID/EX on the normal issue edge and record\n  both source matches there. EX still verifies the load's full forwarded\n  address, alignment and table eligibility. Register the verdict at EX/MEM.\n  A verified hit takes the ordinary adjacent-result bypass. A miss with\n  a matching consumer holds ID/EX until the older load completes. On that\n  edge capture the returned, extended value into each matching operand,\n  let the load retire, and inject one EX/MEM bubble. The held consumer then\n  executes once. For a trapping load keep the pre-load operand values.\n  Gate all consumer side effects, including redirects, predictor training\n  and divider start, until its operands are ready.\n\n  This moves full-address verification off the same-cycle issue decision\n  while retaining the current one-bubble cost of a dependent miss. At the\n  champion's 3,132,302 cycles for ten iterations, a median clock above\n  75.03 MHz clears the replacement margin. Compare both marked cycles and\n  median Fmax because fetch availability may differ across a repair.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Carry the two registered adjacent-source matches to the miss-repair\n      control. Route MEM's qualified write enable and extended result to\n      the held operand registers. Keep instruction and load prediction\n      metadata associated with the consumer throughout the hold.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the combinational EX load-hit decision from fetch stall and\n      flush. Request repair from a valid registered EX/MEM load miss with\n      a valid dependent instruction in ID/EX. Give older dmem waits priority\n      and hold issue through the edge that captures the repaired operands.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Give the two held source registers independent repair enables. A\n      completing load updates each matching source when its write is legal.\n      Hold the consumer's PC, instruction and prediction metadata.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Suppress all EX actions for a consumer awaiting repair. Drain the\n      completed load and bubble EX/MEM on the repair edge so the next\n      execution uses the patched ID/EX operands and can retire only once.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a verified hit and a same-row wrong-tag miss followed by\n      consumers of rs1, rs2 and both. Delay the miss response and check\n      forwarding, RVFI order and data, a dependent branch, a dependent\n      divide, and a misaligned load whose old destination stays live.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
