{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git log --all --oneline --grep='Issue a dependent instruction' | head\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=[json.loads(x) for x in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl') if 'r8s2' in x][-1]\nprint(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nfor c in r['changes']:print(c)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git log --all --oneline --grep='Issue a dependent instruction' | head\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=[json.loads(x) for x in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl') if 'r8s2' in x][-1]\nprint(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nfor c in r['changes']:print(c)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Use a valid, eligible load-table candidate to predict that the adjacent\nconsumer can issue. Keep the existing interlock for a definite miss.\nOn the issue edge, register one bit recording whether either source\nmatches the preceding nonzero destination. In parallel, EX verifies\nthe load's full forwarded word address and alignment. Only an exact\nhit can supply data or suppress the external read.\n\nIf the prediction was wrong, hold the consumer in ID/EX while MEM\ncompletes the older load. On completion, patch each matching source\nwith the extended load result and insert one EX/MEM bubble. A trapping\nload preserves the captured pre-load operands. The consumer then\nexecutes once at its original PC. This costs one bubble on a dependent\nmiss and preserves back-to-back execution on a hit.\n\nA scratch implementation made 189,167 such predictions in ten marked\nCoreMark iterations. It repaired all 31,113 false hits in place and\nfinished in the champion's 3,132,302 cycles with the canonical CRCs.\nGowin placement 1 reached 77.694 MHz, equivalent to 248.04 iterations/s\nat that cycle count. The selftest and three random RVFI comparisons\npassed on both zero-wait and stalled buses.\n\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Drive the issue-time load-use interlock with id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read &&\\n!(candidate.valid && candidate_eligible). On each ID/EX capture,\\nregister rd != 0 && (rd == rs1 || rd == rs2), using the EX destination\\nand the two ID source fields. Hold this bit with ID/EX. Detect repair\\nfrom the registered bit, ID/EX valid and an EX/MEM load with a\\nregistered miss. Send MEM bypass data and independent\\nrs1/rs2 repair enables to ID. Enable each patch only on load completion\\nwith a legal nonzero destination write and a matching source.\\nSuppress load predictor training for a consumer awaiting repair.\\n'}\n{'file': 'rtl/load_predictor.sv', 'description': 'On candidate capture, register the 10-bit read row, MEM write row,\\nupdate enable and scrub-complete bit. Compare the two sampled row\\naddresses in EX so the ID row adder directly feeds the RAM and\\ncapture flops. Veto a read/write collision and retain the live\\nolder-store veto, including across dmem waits.\\n'}\n{'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'OR repair into stall_id so fetch, operand matches and the load probe\\nhold with ID/EX. A waiting older memory operation holds EX/MEM and\\nMEM/WB. Allow the older load to complete on the repair edge.\\n'}\n{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"While held, give rs1_val and rs2_val independent enables to capture\\nthe MEM result. Preserve the consumer's other operand and metadata.\\n\"}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Keep the full hit check local to EX and capture its verdict in\\nEX/MEM. Inhibit divider start, branch redirect and branch training\\nduring repair. On an advancing repair edge, clear EX/MEM valid and\\nside-effect controls. This drains the load and releases its forwarding\\nselects before the held consumer executes with repaired operands.\\n'}\n{'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a row, alternate two RAM pages at the same index, and delay\\nmiss responses. Check an ADD using both repaired sources, a DIVU,\\na store, a branch over a wrong-path store, and a misaligned load\\npreserving its old destination. Assert exact accepted bus transactions,\\nRVFI order and values, and load-to-ADD retirement gaps of two cycles\\non a repaired miss and one on a verified hit.\\n'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
