{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_122","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r9s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261122-003-r9s2\ntitle: Predict the instruction RAM row two issues ahead\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's median Gowin path starts at the successor block RAM, passes through the register file and ends at the load predictor's collision check. Reading a word two instructions before it is needed gives the RAM output a full cycle to reach a register before it drives decode. Indexing the word store by destination PC lets one fill serve multiple control-flow paths.\nhypothesis: |\n  On each accepted issue at PC P, launch a synchronous read for the instruction expected two accepted issues later. Use the word row for P+8 by default. A 128-entry distributed RAM indexed by P[8:2] records exceptions. Each entry holds a valid bit, four more PC tag bits and a ten-bit destination row. Keep two issued PCs' prediction metadata. When a live bus word at Q issues, train the older PC's exception if Q's row differs from its sequential prediction, or clear its previously matched exception if the stream returned to sequential execution. Buffer the fill and training transaction for one cycle.\n  \n  Fill a 1,024-word block RAM at Q[11:2] with the instruction, a valid bit and the full in-window word PC. Read the predicted row on issue, then capture its returned word and tag in fabric registers on the next issue. Both stages hold across stalls. On an imem wait issue the registered word only when its valid full address matches the actual aligned PC in the RAM window. A live bus word always wins. Flush both lookahead stages, history and pending fills on reset or an issued FENCE.I, scrub the word store and retain the existing fence/store interlock. Reject read/write collisions. A redirect never advances issue history and every candidate is still checked against the redirected PC.\n  \n  A scratch build completed ten bracketed iterations in 3,131,081 cycles with all five canonical CRCs and the validation banner. Gowin placement 1 reached 80.366 MHz. The tournament requires a median above 81.93 MHz at that cycle count, so the implementation's clock margin is the open question.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Replace the predecessor-indexed successor word RAM with the two-issue row predictor, destination-indexed word RAM and registered replay candidate. Align prediction history, collision validity and delayed fills with actual issue. Use the existing PC selection, branch resolution and FENCE.I ordering.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise sequential and taken two-issue predictions, an aliased exception, stalls between probe and consumption, and a same-row fill. Check full-PC rejection, ready-bus priority and the first post-FENCE.I instruction after an older stalled code store. Warm the destination RAM before testing consecutive replay-only issues.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r9s2.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
